{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review","id":1468961,"title":"Ravenloft 5th Edition Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-27T02:35:55-08:00","id":1468961,"title":"Ravenloft 5th Edition Review","content":"I just put my hands finally on a copy of Van Richten's Guide to Ravenloft. I love this setting as much as I do WoD and CoD.<br /> <br /> And I'm both happy and furious with this book. There's a lot of good things, there's a lot of terrible things. I didn't read everything yet and I'm not reading it in a proper order, but I can't just keep it to myself, so I'll suffer upon those forums my opinions and comments about everything.<br /> <br /> This may come to be quite less coherent at first than my usual writings, so please forgive if I need more than one try to put my thoughts into order.<br /> <br /> Without further ado, I opened the book and dug directly to the Domains section. To hell with everything else, I want to see what they made with the setting itself.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, they thoroughly eliminated the Core. They eliminated the concept of Ravenloft as a cohesive setting. They made every single Domain into an Island in the Mists and erased politics and history.<br /> <br /> Now, I am upset with that, but I also comprehend. Ravenloft is an awesome toolbox for horror and horror-themed adventures, but sometimes the whole shared history gets in the way. But removing is easier for the ST than adding, and while I have my collection of AD&amp;D and 3rd Edition Ravenloft books to make things right, I'm not happy that new readers aren't being even informed that the possibility exists, that this was a more whole setting.<br /> <br /> Oh, overall I must say I'm torn about the art. There are some very good pieces and others very bad. The maps in general are 5 stars, no complaints, except maybe the new design of some Domains. But the characters... well, lets put it this way: Ravenloft always had a more grounded and classic look to it and I do love the style, but most of the art in this book just isn't like that. That's a particular frustration given that I'm actually quite satisfied with 5th edition's art, maybe more than any other, so it's a huge let down.<br /> <br /> Bad beginning, but not the end yet. My next post will be about the Domains and my thoughts on their write-up, both how it's organized and what they did with each one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T10:23:15-08:00","id":1469001,"title":"","content":"I really didn't like that they shoved Sithicus into oblivion- it was my favorite Domain, with and without Soth, and it fills like they didn't even tried to give a look to the material about the post-Soth setting, which really annoyed me.<br /> <br /> I mean, there were some cool things about it, and I'm fine with some of the changes, but the way they broke Ravenloft into parts and did some revisions which deviated much from the source material felt like they didn't had much respect to the original material, which I really didn't like. Anyway, interested in hearing about your opinions about the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T10:52:22-08:00","id":1469003,"title":"","content":"I liked Van Richten\u2019s overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:36:13-08:00","id":1469029,"title":"","content":"The reduced emphasis on horror frustrated me greatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:41:59-08:00","id":1469031,"title":"","content":"As I understand it the domains were largely isolated in 2nd edition and the Core was more of a 3rd edition thing. Am I incorrect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469029#post1469029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reduced emphasis on horror frustrated me greatly.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you say they de emphasized the horror?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:33:11-08:00","id":1469039,"title":"","content":"I always liked the Core. Especially after 3rd ed tried to make it something where it felt like PCs could actually be from there instead of having to come from elsewhere. <br /> <br /> I like a lot of the ideas in the new book, but I suspect it is more likely to be an additional tool for me trying to use 1st ed Pathfinder to make my own Core or Gothic Earth than used as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:52:44-08:00","id":1469043,"title":"","content":"The thing that personally gets me more than anything else is the whole setup of &quot;the majority of people you encounter in the Domains are basically dour soulless programmed constructs&quot; yet at the same time insisting &quot;but you shouldn't really care, now have your characters get up to heroic horror-themed adventure where they risk their lives to save pretty much on average soulless constructs!&quot; It basically emphasizes Ravenloft as not much more than something to use for &quot;Weekend at Strahd's&quot; or the like, instead of being a setting in its own right.<br /> <br /> They took the philosophical concept of a p-zombie, built an entire setting around it, and rolled on from there. And I guess that would be fine if Ravenloft is basically meant for little more in 5e than a relatively brief adventure sequence where your characters are dumped into Ravenloft, do a thing, and then get dumped back onto their world, but the book wants to have it both ways and talk about characters like they can be meaningfully from these domains and like they can be actual valid settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T17:20:45-08:00","id":1469047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469001#post1469001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the way they broke Ravenloft into parts and did some revisions which deviated much from the source material felt like they didn't had much respect to the original material</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the main bad point in a nutshell: they didn't respect the original material. And respecting the original material isn't bad in itself, but doing it so thoroughly is a disrespect to the players. For new players because it closes avenues, for old players because it disregard their previous investment with the setting.<br /> <br /> It is a huge problem, I have to say. Time and again I read here things that make me feel bad with how they simply disregarded the past and retconned everything without giving two fucks to the reader.<br /> <br /> Now, some people complained that the problem was the book making an effort to be more inclusive. I thoroughly disagree. Undoubtedly the book did made this effort and I find it welcome, and certainly it was rushed and it shows. But it doesn't have to be bad and some pieces do that very well. The problem isn't the effort itself, but the attitude of disregard for the past, and it isn't really tied to the inclusive effort.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>NATURE OF RAVENLOFT</b></u></i><br /> <br /> Many interesting bits here. I like the simpler rules for traveling the Mists, but the table needs serious revisions. Currently you have 20% chance of leaving a domain against 49% of going back and 31% of Mist shenanigans that end up with rolling in the table again. Good idea, bad execution.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Mist Talismans are simply excellent, how didn't they had this idea before? Simple, elegant, colorful. Brilliant.<br /> <br /> The section on magic was another let down, although without looking at the rest of the book I'm not sure yet how it is or isn't affected by Powers Checks or other such mechanics. But while touching on the matter of Magic's rarity and corruption in Ravenloft at least recognizes the phenomena, the lack of more details on how to use it, and later the lack of examples on those takes in the Domains' write-ups seriously harms the book. The parts on souls and planar magic are on spot.<br /> <br /> For mundane life the write-up is short but mostly on spot. Currency was just unnecessary (same thing as everywhere else), I like the presentation of Language as starting with Common being Common and Domain languages as an optional rule. Although one I'll frequently use, the number of languages and complexity of tracking where they're spoken, while fun for a GM that wants to dwell on this like me, is an unnecessary constraint for most campaigns.<br /> <br /> Religion, on the other hand, was butchered. The complexity of religion in the setting was downplayed to its most simplistic form and Ezra was simplified to the extreme, its history and interplay completely ignored. I'm yet to decide what I think of the lack of mention to the forbiddance of gods in the Domains, so I'll give that taking it off isn't necessarily a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>WRITE-UP STRUCTURE</i></u></b><br /> <br /> I like their presentation here. I don't think a more detailed description of any Domain is necessary, their focus on practical information for the GM is all good and well. But again, they should have added a paragraph or side box about where to find more detailed information. On top of that, while they say it doesn't have to be so, the write-ups will really lack ideas on how to use a domain without bringing the Dark Lord as the centerpiece of the adventure.<br /> <br /> They did, though, and that's a plus, made it overall clearer how much the Dark Lord is a presence in the domain even when as background, and how to convey this notion, which is something good. Avoiding giving the Darklord complex stats and just focus on their unique effects was also quite ok.<br /> <br /> Now I'll take a breath before diving in our first Domains. I'll try to make two or three each time, so soon we'll see Barovia, Bluetspur and Borca. Each I have some serious thoughts to share, but the quick spoiler: Barovia has the worst Strahd's art I ever seen (but arguably the best Sergei's), Bluetspur was kind of abandoned in the 3rd edition and this was a far better rendition, the Dark Twins have been heavily altered, with positives and negatives to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469031#post1469031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it the domains were largely isolated in 2nd edition and the Core was more of a 3rd edition thing. Am I incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you are.<br /> <br /> The Core is the main feature of the setting since the original Black Box campaign setting &quot;Ravenloft: Realm of Terror&quot; from 1990. That remained true for all three subsequent iterations thereafter, the Red Box from 1994, Domains of Dread from 1997 and 3rd Edition Campaign Setting from 2001.<br /> <br /> What was new to 3rd edition, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> said, was the presentation of the Core as somewhere the PCs could hail from, which is a take they kept in place, fortunately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469003#post1469003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked Van Richten\u2019s overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you did, it's Ravenloft!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469039#post1469039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like a lot of the ideas in the new book, but I suspect it is more likely to be an additional tool for me trying to use 1st ed Pathfinder to make my own Core or Gothic Earth than used as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, while I do intend to use it for 3.5 and 5th edition, it is also basically a tool box to accompany any of the previous setting books instead of to be used as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469043#post1469043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that personally gets me more than anything else is the whole setup of &quot;the majority of people you encounter in the Domains are basically dour soulless programmed constructs&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a simpler way they found to cover an old question in the setting.<br /> <br /> Since its inception, it's a fact in Ravenloft the Dark Powers create people. They populate domains with people made from scratch, full with false memories, especially at a domain's first appearance, although sometimes after that.<br /> <br /> Also, those peoples are created with a lack of curiosity that serves well to keep the <i>Status Quo</i> of the Domains despite anything. This is an important aspect, as more willing peoples could unravel the prisons of the Dark Lords, AKA ruin the theme.<br /> <br /> What to make out of this? In the greater D&amp;D cosmology, souls are a factual thing, and for the Dark Powers Free Will is an important thing. Evil is only truly damning if chosen of your own accord, and so is Good.<br /> <br /> Not that I especially like this soulless setup, but I do not interpret it as them being dull or just constructs, but as a lack of some fundamental spark that could drive them to other choices - and an easy way to avoid trickier questions about from where those people came from.<br /> <br /> Basically they're people, they have feelings, goals, hopes, rights. But as soulless they are also &quot;standard&quot;, they lack drive to enact actual changes to their lives and tend to conform to local stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T17:46:47-08:00","id":1469050,"title":"","content":"I once saw the suggested idea that all of the original inhabitants of Ravenloft could be souls sentenced to some sort of Purgatory-like punishment/crucible. I wish I could remember where though. Never been entirely sure how I feel about the idea either. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T19:24:25-08:00","id":1469061,"title":"","content":"5th edition Ravenloft was okay, but I was thoroughly disappointed that they shattered the setting. I ran a Ravenloft game about 4 years ago using the 5th edition ruleset and the 3rd edition setting (the players were part of a mercenary company that sold their services to various Dark Lords, which served as an excuse for traveling around the world). If I were to run another Ravenloft game I would absolutely stick with the 2nd/3rd edition setting with Ravenloft as a collection of domains all linked together by the Mist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T20:45:04-08:00","id":1469066,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine has made a supplement for vampires that was put out on the Dungeon Master's Guild back in September. If it appeals to you, purchase a copy. He pretty much did what WOTC refused to do...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/370916/Van-Richtens-Ecology-of-Vampires\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/8957/370916.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/370916/Van-Richtens-Ecology-of-Vampires\" target=\"_blank\"> Van Richten's Ecology of Vampires - Dungeon Masters Guild | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/370916/Van-Richtens-Ecology-of-Vampires\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/370916/Van-Richtens-Ecology-of-Vampires </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Van Richten's Ecology of Vampires - \"On that terrible day, I swore myself to a new career: the pursuit and destruction of those creatures such as the one t </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T21:23:21-08:00","id":1469068,"title":"","content":"Apropos to nothing, I keep coming back to the idea that I really want to run Ravenloft (or something very close to it) in what I call The Era of Tricorn Hats, ie the equivalent of around the time of the Seven Years War to the French Revolution/British Regency era (Brotherhood of the Wolf, Frankenstein, etc.). This is probably why I keep wanting to use Pathfinder, as it has things like Investigator, Swashbuckler, Alchemist, and Mesmorist as already made classes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T22:51:49-08:00","id":1469070,"title":"","content":"For me, one of the coolest thing about Ravenloft is how incredibly diverse the Dark Domains are. You have domains populated by literal cavemen who eek by in caves and fight dinosaurs. And then you have a domain like Lamordia which is modeled off of a mixture of post-Gothic Germany and Victorian England. Or you have Odiare, which is a 16th century Italian city from literal Earth. And of course it's rather easy to make a new Domain to have whatever you want in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T00:18:51-08:00","id":1469074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469050#post1469050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once saw the suggested idea that all of the original inhabitants of Ravenloft could be souls sentenced to some sort of Purgatory-like punishment/crucible. I wish I could remember where though. Never been entirely sure how I feel about the idea either. \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideas like that always floated about. They could had just kept silent about the matter, and that would keep the mystery, but wouldn't quell the question. One way or another this has always been a thorny aspect of the setting, coming to terms on how the Mists have so much power over the population while keeping Free Will intact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469066#post1469066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He pretty much did what WOTC refused to do...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/370916/Van-Richtens-Ecology-of-Vampires\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...gy-of-Vampires</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll maybe take a look later.<br /> <br /> Before I begin, one thing I think I forget, commenting on the new rules for Closing the Borders. They're reasonable, but should have been done more customizable. Doesn't have to be fancy, the Ability used for the save should depend on the Domain and it could have one or two optional effects on par with causing 1d6 damage.<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>BAROVIA</i></u></b><br /> <br /> Initial presentation pretty standard. I must say: I like that they don't dwell too much on descriptions of the land since they have a very good map for it. That means conveying information efficiently. What draws my attention, though, is that they state that &quot;many&quot; residents believe Strahd to be a vampire. This not only departs from the original description, I think it is a bad decision.<br /> <br /> Not to say that Strahd being a vampire should be a big reveal. I mean, even if your players know nothing about him, he's pretty obvious and in fact in the OG setting this was common knowledge outside Barovia.<br /> <br /> But the local ignorance wasn't just a joke, but a subtle yet effective storytelling device. It shows Strahd isn't <i>defined</i> by being a vampire, but is a vampire as a development of being who he is. It reminds the players that, for the Barovians, Strahd is first and foremost their lord. The land belongs to him, depends on his governance, pays him tribute. And yet this quite mundane figure is called as a Devil. He doesn't need supernatural powers or proclivities to be extremely evil.<br /> <br /> Another problem is the general abandonment of old names, with many established characters from before being changed for new ones for no reason at all. Same everything, just new names, usually variations on the name of the villages themselves.<br /> <br /> Mostly the locations have been ported from <i>Curse of Strahd</i> rather than from previous editions of the setting. This was expected, but unfortunate. Just as in <i>Expedition to Castle Ravenloft</i>, what works in the closed adventure module does not works so well in a broader setting. For Krezk it meant replacing the Sanctuary of the First Light with the Abbey of St Markovia. The former, a seat for a religious movement markedly Barovian. The later, a fast reference to the old Domain of Markovia, based on similar themes to the Abbey (Dr. Moreau) and background of the 1996's module <i>Neither Man Nor Beast</i>.<br /> <br /> Vallaki was completely changed. Although I don't find the plot hook bad, it severely lacks versatility and potential compared to its previous description and on top makes little sense: how's it that a town so well positioned is the &quot;isolated&quot; one? The village of Barovia is par of the course, and the Amber Temple is the crux of a plot I don't like and don't see relevant outside that one adventure.<br /> <br /> Ravenloft the Setting is a very different beast from Ravenloft the adventure. That has been true since the dawn of the setting. The land of Barovia must lend itself to much more possibilities of exploration here, and keeping to the colorful but shallow plot lines from CoS wasn't the best idea. That spot with the Amber Temple could have been used for a number of other curios.<br /> <br /> Strahd's write-up is good, save for the aforementioned plot with the Amber Temple. He somewhat lacks the hint of madness that completed his figure so well, but not completely and the text is pretty good. That art, though, oh, my goodness, <b>that's painfully awful!</b> I literally must make an effort to stay in the page of that damned thing.<br /> <br /> The rest of it is about adventures in Barovia and Tatyana. It focus too much on using Strahd as the game's villain and Tatyana as a foil against him, this is already covered by CoS. The bits about using any or both of them in less direct ways are very good, but could have used more space, it should also have more options related to other Barovian villains.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>BLUETSPUR</u></i></b><br /> <br /> Now we have a positively good change. And a change of pace, as definitely I have to be less thorough on my examination.<br /> <br /> After the original 1992's module <i>Thoughts of Darkness</i>, few to no Ravenloft book managed to do much with Bluetspur. It is maybe one of the best uses of Illithids in D&amp;D, doing what Illithids should do. The problem is how to put more on it than Illithids being Illithids.<br /> <br /> I dare to say this is one of the best tries, maybe the best. It conveys quickly the feel of the place, its dangers, and ways of using it. Indeed I dare to say that the advice and rules on intruding Bluetspur in other places is the best on how to use it outside the original module I ever saw, quite opposite to what they did in Barovia.<br /> <br /> The God-Brain has also been a thorn in the setting, as nothing seemed to justify this Elder Brain becoming a Darklord and others not. There is a net book semi-official theory from the 3rd edition authors about it being a mix of minds with a human Psion as the dominant one and the true Darklord, but I think this write-up here work far better.<br /> <br /> Since I did so much on Barovia this time, I'll stop for now, managed two domains. Next time Borca and my pros and cons for the new take on the Dark Twins; Carnival and my absolute rage against what they did to one of my favorites; and if time lets me, Darkon and why it's actually a now classic batch of Azalin's shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T04:28:42-08:00","id":1469086,"title":"","content":"On the subject of soulless people- the thing I didn't like is how they actually spelled it out. Like, I mean, I still remember how dumbfounded I was when I read Knight of the Black Rose where a whole Domain was created around Lord Soth, people included. From where did they came from? Are they real or not? Can the Dark Powers create people out of nothing? This was just so weird and interesting to think about which left a lasting impression on me for years. By spelling &quot;oh, those people are just soulless fictions created from the shadowstuff of the Shadowfell&quot; (because they have also decided to officially stuck Ravenloft in the Shadowfell because of, well, reasons?), it both removes that weirdness and mystery which I found so intriguing and, in a way, creates a very uncomfortable situation- because if everything, including Ravenloft's people, are nothing but props meant for the Darklords to keep the show going, then it is ok that the Darklords will torture them, as they exist only to be tormented and to torment the Darklords in their hellish prison. It also makes it ok to discard whole Domains into the oblivion once the Dark Powers are done with the Darklord, because, well, they served their purpose and are not relevant anymore. I mean, sure, soulless people are just people- but when they were created to suffer and it is their whole purpose, it takes something, and could, in a way, justify that it is ok for the Darklord to do as they wish, because it keeps them in their prison and those people only exist as an extension of their own twisted desires.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I really don't like it. I don't remember if it was mention in Van Richten, but the concept of soulless people took a lot from the setting without giving much in return, imo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T13:37:09-08:00","id":1469119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469086#post1469086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember if it was mention in Van Richten, but the concept of soulless people took a lot from the setting without giving much in return, imo</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to agree, despite not being so bothered.<br /> <br /> But that's also a lot about my own philosophy. For me the idea that causing them to suffer is ok just because it is their defined purpose doesn't hold, and I think this is kind of the deal with them: their nature <b>does not</b> make them less deserving of kindness, and using it to justify your actions is itself a hallmark of evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469086#post1469086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they have also decided to officially stuck Ravenloft in the Shadowfell because of, well, reasons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually as a natural development of previous decisions.<br /> <br /> WotC has been trying to shove Ravenloft out of their way for a long time, to be actually honest here. They made the Shadowfell to cover the same general role in 4th Edition and had been avoiding the setting itself like the plague. This actually goes back to 3rd edition, when they decided to not renew WW's license for the setting despite ongoing publication schedule then published the <i>Expedition</i> module in lieu of the rest of the Gazetteer series.<br /> <br /> Officially, despite nothing in the license impeding the module's publications.<br /> <br /> They made the Shadowfell and thoroughly shoved the concept of Domains of Dread there, since 4th edition. They published already eight Domains of Dread since then without mention to Ravenloft, and republished a number of Ravenloft Domains in the same manner including Barovia, Kalidnay and, IIRC, Stauton Bluffs.<br /> <br /> Yet, here we are. The setting have a strong following and the <a href=\"http://fraternityofshadows.com/wiki/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">Mistipedia</a> is still maintained and updated (although not every entry is of the same quality). At this point the structure of the setting is already anchored at the Shadowfell, though, so it is understandable that they preferred to keep it there.<br /> <br /> But enough of my ramblings, we have a tour to continue.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>BORCA</u></i></b><br /> <br /> I'm very satisfied with the overview of the land. Everything seems in place, and although they didn't mention that it is the birthplace of Ezra's faith, the Great Cathedral is still there, it's alliance with the Morninglord changed to the new Ulmist Inquisition. Excellent writing, no complains at all.<br /> <br /> Jumping to the session about Adventures and following tips on using Borca, it's also very good. With the sole exception of <i>Intrigue in Borca</i>starting out kind of confusing and aimless, the write-up closes with very good advice, this time with many helpful tips to use other villains and plots than the Darklords.<br /> <br /> But I left those two for last for a reason. The Dark Twins have been a fixture in the setting for quite a long time. And here they got significantly changed. Some of it is just for the sake of change, or rather for the sake of defacing all previous editions as it seems. Some of it though, for good or ill, was to tweak the ways the two can be used in the table.<br /> <br /> Changes for the sake of change include making their history so that Borca is their shared domain from start. It doesn't really use up less of a word count than necessary to instead quickly summarize Ivana's inheritance from her mother and previous Darklord, and the merge with Ivan's original Domain of Dorvinia. Those details change nothing really, but help give a sense of dept to the place.<br /> <br /> Now, Ivana has a good chunk of her history reworked and is turned into a very different person in terms of how she relates to people. Her whole trope is changed from the Borgia-style Black Widow to the business woman that's never taken seriously. The poison is still kept as her signature MO, though. I'm torn on this because I do miss parts of her backstory, especially the role of Camille as the Legacy Villain, but on the other hand I <b>am</b> tired of the whole <i>this woman is evil because romance shenanigans</i> stuff. Now it does keep her love story as trigger, but her motivation is more interesting.<br /> <br /> On Ivan things are far more complicated. The changes are almost complete, and I don't like the new backstory that much. It abandons his original specific but exquisite murders (murdering the mother for the giggles, murdering the sister and her family when she have a son, making the incestuous overtones more clear), in favor of plain, sweeping mass murder. Cute, but Strahd already did it, and this time Ivana did too, it's getting old.<br /> <br /> The new Ivan is unrecognizable, but the old Ivan was too similar on practice to Ivana. In a sense they worked better as obvious counterparts, but now they offer more varied opportunities. He moved from being an inferior copy of Ivana with Gluttony instead of Lust as trademark to being like a Batman villain, Penguin mainly. Not sure if I like it, but among the changes made, it could easily be far worse, and the Domain itself can still work in the old style.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>THE CARNIVAL</b></u></i><br /> <br /> Oh, my goodness... my poor Isolde, what they did to you...<br /> <br /> So, given the constraints of being a short write-up I can totally forgive not delving into the tragedies of the troupers backstories, and the open-ended short description for each one isn't a bad thing. The Litwick Market is a new feature, and since it adds conflict I'm not against it. The Adventures section is short and very basic, though, and no mention goes to the Skurra or the Twisting, which is understandable but sad.<br /> <br /> And at the core of it Isolde got completely revamped. The new Isolde is just a retired Paladin paying attention to the antics of a sword that isn't even all that committed to evil to justify being a Darklord.<br /> <br /> I mean, Nepenthe isn't a bad character. It would make a fair addition to the wandering pseudo-domain by itself. But in the end, they should just not had put Carnival at all in the book, not to make it like this. With the themes they actually used, they could either have revamped Scaena in similar ways (I do like that Domain, but it has been abandoned for a long time and needs in fact a revamping to have broader use and appeal), or the old Shadowlands cluster, since Nepenthe is a mashup of Ebonbane and Elena Faith-hold anyways.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>DARKON</u></i></b><br /> <br /> Azalin Rex, the oldest and most powerful Lich in Ravenloft, disappeared at the culmination of a magical ritual infused with insane amounts of energy collected at the end of a long and complex conspiracy, in an event known throughout the land by a grandiose, ominous name. The land of Darkon is suffering under the swift and terrible energies released, magic scars left behind and causing havoc. No one knows whats happening or what if any future awaits for the most expansive kingdom in the Mists. The vampires of the Kargat conspire in the shadows and crush the population under their ruthless bullying and incentive to betrayal and violence. Castle Avernus is the center point of danger and death. Huge swaths of this land that weren't a problem in previous editions just became inhabitable.<br /> <br /> In other words, Thursday.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that the domain isn't changed or that I liked it. Huge swaths of land are missing, although none that really matters. The Kargat is decentralized in their current infighting, which adds conflict but removes the sting of their efficiency. I think the domain could have taken other turns.<br /> <br /> Yet, Darkon is one of the simplest domains to use because you can throw any fantasy staple of D&amp;D there and take it at face value, no need to adapt. Is a pretty standard fantasy land, minus warring nations, plus more undead. It's a refreshing presence sometimes, and its size contrasts with the sense of claustrophobia and isolation typical to other domains. All that remains as true as ever.<br /> <br /> The option of your players visiting Azalin's castle frozen mid-explosion was a nice touch, so much better that he isn't home. Il Aluk is back without any explanation, which is bad but expected. The sample contenders for his throne are interesting, diverse and cover multiple styles of game. I liked the new Baron Metus pretty much.<br /> <br /> My only true complaining, the nitpicks I mentioned, first that Azalin was also unnecessarily changed. He has always been presented as a Dr. Doom-like king: a ruthless tyrant, but also a competent ruler that aims for the benefit of his kingdom. Unlike Strahd he's not the worse evil for his subjects, as his torment is actually his inability to part ways with his duties for fear of seeing his legacy destroyed by less competent hands. Azalin is a good king 'cause he hates being the king, yet other threats in Darkon keep him in the throne.<br /> <br /> Second and a bit more serious, the Adventure section focus completely on stories revolving around Darkon's current ongoing apocalypse. Considering that this is an ongoing matter that can actually take centuries to come to a resolution, and they actually implemented changes that give so much to do in the mean time, I find it a disservice to their own work here to not give a good look at other options and let the Shroud be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T16:28:00-08:00","id":1469131,"title":"","content":"As long as we got this thread up, out of curiosity, what's everyone's favorite Dark Doman/Darklord? <br /> <br /> I've always been a fan of the Wildlands and King Crocodile. It's kind of got that evil fairytale/Disney vibe with all of the intelligent animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T12:21:56-08:00","id":1469188,"title":"","content":"King Crocodile was a really good one. I think of the originals, it would probably be Jacqueline Renier, for her cunning and overall competence. And I kind of enjoy how the domain is mostly fine, but has this perpetual rot under the surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T21:48:53-08:00","id":1469227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469131#post1469131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as we got this thread up, out of curiosity, what's everyone's favorite Dark Doman/Darklord?<br /> <br /> I've always been a fan of the Wildlands and King Crocodile. It's kind of got that evil fairytale/Disney vibe with all of the intelligent animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a hard question for me, very hard. But I have a weak spot for stories that make power level irrelevant, approachable and interesting for everyone. Things like low level characters having pretty mundane audiences with Strahd or Azalin.<br /> <br /> So my particular favorite is probably the cursed theater Scaena and Lemont Sediam Juste. You can go wild with it, challenge your PCs with whatever impossible task you want, and still have them survive. Until Lemont decides to burn the place, that is.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>DEMENTLIEU</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">What the hell. That was\u2026 interesting?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">They thoroughly changed Dementlieu, and the result is a mixed bag. This is one of the original domains from the 1990\u2019s Black Box, and Dominic D\u2019Honaire one of the most classic villains in Ravenloft. Also, I think one that would serve better at their current style of focusing more on the Darklord, as one of the main shticks here used to be the sheer reach of his web of manipulation and conspiracy (or that of his enemies).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But this time we have a sweeping change with the place dotted with references, good and bad. The first joke is the whole thing with building the new Dementlieu completely around the title Masque of the Red Death (the Ravenloft-related setting of Gothic Earth). Yeah, funny\u2026 the domain is far more single-note and ultimately rid of the old theme of conspiracy and its cosmopolitan air. One thing I understand is that as a whole old Dementlieu would be more hurt than most by becoming an Island of Terror. The whole \u201cSinderela With a Twist\u201d is too much on the nose, both on Saidra\u2019s backstory and on the part of the Three Odd Gables. And of course, the domain hold little surprise after a time, since it makes a point to not have many real secrets, in opposition to old version.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On the other side, the new theme definitely isn\u2019t bad per se. Actually, it isn\u2019t bad at all, just a little repetitive. This whole thing would work wonderfully as a new development along with old-style Dementlieu\u2026 and we may have it! Ok, kinda. For the trained eye the hints of the old domain are all over the place, and they made a good job in their selections of places to present, adventure advice and guiding the GM to use the Grand Masquerade as an event and plot device without making it solely about the duchess. Indeed, I must praise how much they put in it tools and ideas for adventures unrelated to Saidra even while keeping her presence overwhelmingly relevant. It is genuinely good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">My specific observations: the domain went through the same thing Zherisia went through after the Conjunction, shrinking from its former size to just the capital. Yet, the map is almost the same. Port-a-Lucine now occupies the whole map of Dementlieu, and the two bays are still there. Some features of the kingdom were integrated into the city. The ditched Chateufaux from the map, which is a shame, but they added a wonderful mystery with everyone still referencing a place that doesn\u2019t exists. The Cathedral are still in place, expected and ok. Lord Von Aubrecker is absent from the domain, but it seems he went back to Lamordia, and by the second idea in the Adventures Table we get that Dominic is actually still present! He\u2019s a patient in a hospital and still have power to manipulate and dominate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I have to part ways saying that although I disagree with the narrower scope of the domain, I ended up liking it a lot. A few details are the difference between utter disrespect and a change that can actually pick the interest of an of fan, and here the latter was accomplished. Despite a little on the nose, Saidra is a good character, and the idea of a place where evil doesn\u2019t even hide, yet people are whiling to mingle with monsters to pretend for a better, but normal life is priceless. I won\u2019t be so kind in our next step, Falkovnia.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Correcting format 11-30-2021, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T12:45:02-08:00","id":1469413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469003#post1469003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked Van Richten\u2019s overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you look for old Ravenloft books. Not in the sense of not using the 5th ed one, just because they're also good to add stuff to your games and most of the good parts aren't bound to any particular game system.<br /> <br /> Particularly anything else that start with &quot;Van Richten Guide to&quot;. Those are in-character books about several subjects and full of really interesting ideas on how to apply their themes to games. They're wonderful.<br /> <br /> This new one is, curiously, the only book with such title that isn't in-character.<br /> <br /> Now back to the review.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>FALKOVNIA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The original Falkovnia would be the Domain most hurt by becoming an Island of Terror. Vlad Drakov is a failed conqueror, he thoroughly needs neighbors to conquer. Of course, the Island could provide this on itself anyways and still be smaller than Darkon, but other domains are a better fit. Drakov never realized his own predicament.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Now, the new Falkovnia does works well in this Island state. I just don\u2019t like it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Seriously, an entire domain the size of Falkovnia dedicated solely to a constant theme of Zombie Apocalypse? This could too easily be inserted as a plot without dedicating a main domain to it, much less sacrifice the place that best had the themes of totalitarianism and military state.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I don\u2019t have much to add. The domain is well written and the hooks work well. The section on conducting the monthly siege is worth reading all by itself to conduct similar operations, and reminds me a little Legend of Five Rings 4</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> Edition\u2019s rules for mass combat, which are pretty good for their focus on the PCs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Vladeska will, by itself, hurt a lot of players. Screw them. She has the exact same backstory as Vlad, nothing changes beyond the domain focus itself. She would work fantastically well as his daughter and potential successor, maybe holding against this apocalypse in a remote area of the domain or a new domain all hers. And the art of her fighting the undead is very good, not perfect, but definitely good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>HAR\u2019AKIR</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Another old domain from the Black Box, another batch of deep changes I don\u2019t quite get. First of all, why they changed the pantheon? I mean, it can\u2019t be for safety reasons, they already have the Egyptian Pantheon in 5</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> edition and they say it out loud here. Ankhtepot\u2019s story also don\u2019t had anything particularly problematic. At the worse it had standard vilifying of Set, but that was nothing too relevant (it only mattered a little for his enemies after becoming Darklord, actually).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">That puzzles me, but aside that it doesn\u2019t matter a lot. They really delved into the theme of false religion here, but it isn\u2019t hard to change it back and still use most of the write-up. Or not change, it isn\u2019t criminally bad, just weird. That aside, the domain itself is better defined and described than on most previous iterations, and this description is very good. Places like the Breaths and the Bent Pyramid add a lot to it, as does the Labyrinth and the four oases instead of just Muhar. Muhar\u2019s population soared ten fold: it\u2019s now 3 thousand souls. Less quaint than before, but more useful as story device.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But not the same can be said of the characters. Those should be the meat of any Ravenloft write-up and we got changes that made everyone boring and same-ish. Some old names are still here, likeIsu Rehkotep, Senmet and Nephyr, but now they\u2019re all bland and most are just Ankhtepot\u2019s servants. The Darklord\u2019s history changed completely, also. It isn\u2019t completely bad, but it kind of defeats its purpose. The new lore have him first a far more empathetic soul and hardly Darklord material, then he gets a punishment that\u2019s out of proportion for reasons, and finally he decides to create a false religion for reasons, since he isn\u2019t actually getting much out of it, it goes counter to his depiction in the background and current, and plays no role in his ultimate goal of facing his gods judgment again.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Finishing this analysis, the Adventure ideas and the advice for using Ankhtepot\u2019s Ka are good, but not by much. It\u2019s flatly below the standards from most previous write-ups. The Ankhtepot Reborn table is especially bad, four suggestions for ending the quest that are either anti-climatic or predictable and avoid any actual change. Either Ankhtepot remains in power, leaves power but nothing changes, must be reinstated to power because change is bad, or the GM pushes the Apocalypse butom.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>HAZLAN</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Ok, this is the Domain that suffered more changes so far. Others had sweeping changes but are still arguably the same or similar place, Hazlan is completely unrecognizable and Hazlik almost as much. On the good side, I can say that the rules on wild magic are interesting and the general idea of a kingdom-size arcane laboratory gone wild is interesting. As in Har\u2019Akir, a lot of useful places for adventures were added.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But they stripped the domain of its most interesting social problems. Hazlan dealt with oppression and racism, and Hazlik was hell bent on committing trans-universal genocide. Not anymore. His complex relationship with genre and transsexuality is also gone. At least he\u2019s still gay, but outside that he\u2019s just a simplified version of old Azalin in everything but body. And his tattoos are now golden and mean traitor or something.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Formatting 12-02-2021, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avat