/span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>HAR\u2019AKIR</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Another old domain from the Black Box, another batch of deep changes I don\u2019t quite get. First of all, why they changed the pantheon? I mean, it can\u2019t be for safety reasons, they already have the Egyptian Pantheon in 5</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> edition and they say it out loud here. Ankhtepot\u2019s story also don\u2019t had anything particularly problematic. At the worse it had standard vilifying of Set, but that was nothing too relevant (it only mattered a little for his enemies after becoming Darklord, actually).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">That puzzles me, but aside that it doesn\u2019t matter a lot. They really delved into the theme of false religion here, but it isn\u2019t hard to change it back and still use most of the write-up. Or not change, it isn\u2019t criminally bad, just weird. That aside, the domain itself is better defined and described than on most previous iterations, and this description is very good. Places like the Breaths and the Bent Pyramid add a lot to it, as does the Labyrinth and the four oases instead of just Muhar. Muhar\u2019s population soared ten fold: it\u2019s now 3 thousand souls. Less quaint than before, but more useful as story device.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But not the same can be said of the characters. Those should be the meat of any Ravenloft write-up and we got changes that made everyone boring and same-ish. Some old names are still here, likeIsu Rehkotep, Senmet and Nephyr, but now they\u2019re all bland and most are just Ankhtepot\u2019s servants. The Darklord\u2019s history changed completely, also. It isn\u2019t completely bad, but it kind of defeats its purpose. The new lore have him first a far more empathetic soul and hardly Darklord material, then he gets a punishment that\u2019s out of proportion for reasons, and finally he decides to create a false religion for reasons, since he isn\u2019t actually getting much out of it, it goes counter to his depiction in the background and current, and plays no role in his ultimate goal of facing his gods judgment again.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Finishing this analysis, the Adventure ideas and the advice for using Ankhtepot\u2019s Ka are good, but not by much. It\u2019s flatly below the standards from most previous write-ups. The Ankhtepot Reborn table is especially bad, four suggestions for ending the quest that are either anti-climatic or predictable and avoid any actual change. Either Ankhtepot remains in power, leaves power but nothing changes, must be reinstated to power because change is bad, or the GM pushes the Apocalypse butom.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>HAZLAN</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Ok, this is the Domain that suffered more changes so far. Others had sweeping changes but are still arguably the same or similar place, Hazlan is completely unrecognizable and Hazlik almost as much. On the good side, I can say that the rules on wild magic are interesting and the general idea of a kingdom-size arcane laboratory gone wild is interesting. As in Har\u2019Akir, a lot of useful places for adventures were added.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But they stripped the domain of its most interesting social problems. Hazlan dealt with oppression and racism, and Hazlik was hell bent on committing trans-universal genocide. Not anymore. His complex relationship with genre and transsexuality is also gone. At least he\u2019s still gay, but outside that he\u2019s just a simplified version of old Azalin in everything but body. And his tattoos are now golden and mean traitor or something.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll check it out. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T00:01:52-08:00","id":1469631,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons I always liked Falkovia in the original and d20 editions is that it was a kind of low key place where the horror was less from ghost and goblins and more from the fact it was ruled by someone with the worst traits of Vlad the Impaler and Ivan the Terrible. I worry that &quot;zombie apocalypse&quot; might detract from that. If anything, it always struck me as one of the domains that could do folk horror really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T09:15:35-08:00","id":1469649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469631#post1469631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons I always liked Falkovia in the original and d20 editions is that it was a kind of low key place where the horror was less from ghost and goblins and more from the fact it was ruled by someone with the worst traits of Vlad the Impaler and Ivan the Terrible. I worry that &quot;zombie apocalypse&quot; might detract from that. If anything, it always struck me as one of the domains that could do folk horror really well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falkovnia, Hazlan and Nova Vaasa are domains that work especially well with this kind of folk horror. Even with the supernatural forces at hand, the real horror does not come from them, but on the totalitarian states they built.<br /> <br /> This was lost in the new versions. Hazlan wasn't about magic, it was about racism, with a racist tyrant focused on Nazi-style research and a pogrom for genocide, curiously against his own politically dominant ethnicity. Drakov was at once Tepes and Ivan, but also Hitler, Stalin and Pol Pot.<br /> <br /> Heck, they even removed his branding of the peoples of Falkovnia, now it is just a tattoo the loyal troops make somewhere in their bodies. Yeah, I know branding people like cattle isn't a good thing to do. That's why it was a villain doing that, one almost devoid of redeeming qualities.<br /> <br /> But on another note, I'm not sure if the current model is working. I have already the text on I'Cath done and am ready to write Kalakeri and Kartakass. But is this model of commenting each Domain with my usual verborragic length working?<br /> <br /> What do you say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T12:11:46-08:00","id":1469657,"title":"","content":"I think that the change at Har'Akir's pantheon was due to them trying to distance it from &quot;outdated mummy stereotypes&quot; (I think those were the words they used?). Like, they decided that having a Egyptian themed Domain was outdated/offensive/whatever and wanted to revised it into something more &quot;high fantasy&quot; kind of thing. Basically, it wasn't that the pantheon itself was problematic, but that they decided that having a &quot;Egyptian/Mummy Domain&quot; was problematic, and so they did their best to distance it from its origin. Which is a choice. Not sure if the best choice, but they did suffered from some bad PR during that time and it was supposedly part of them having &quot;new and improved attitude&quot; or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:21:32-08:00","id":1469670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469657#post1469657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the change at Har'Akir's pantheon was due to them trying to distance it from &quot;outdated mummy stereotypes&quot; (I think those were the words they used?). Like, they decided that having a Egyptian themed Domain was outdated/offensive/whatever and wanted to revised it into something more &quot;high fantasy&quot; kind of thing. Basically, it wasn't that the pantheon itself was problematic, but that they decided that having a &quot;Egyptian/Mummy Domain&quot; was problematic, and so they did their best to distance it from its origin. Which is a choice. Not sure if the best choice, but they did suffered from some bad PR during that time and it was supposedly part of them having &quot;new and improved attitude&quot; or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense and it is probably the reason behind some changes in it and in other domains, but for Har'Akir it doesn't actually add up.<br /> <br /> Again, the problem is that they <i>outright say it was the Egyptian Pantheon</i>. It is in a side box in the domain's write-up. Ankhtepot was a priest of the Egyptian Pantheon and the Akiri worshiped the Egyptian Pantheon when the domain formed.<br /> <br /> Instead of avoiding this particular stereotype, they double down on it. And the new Akiri Pantheon isn't worked as a fantasy religion, but outright as a fake religion. And the lost temples of the Egyptian Pantheon are still there to be discovered by adventurers.<br /> <br /> So while they certainly developed Har'Akir beyond just being Egypt as seen by the British, it is still pretty much Egypt. And it actually has more mummies than original Har'Akir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:37:54-08:00","id":1469671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469649#post1469649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falkovnia, Hazlan and Nova Vaasa are domains that work especially well with this kind of folk horror. Even with the supernatural forces at hand, the real horror does not come from them, but on the totalitarian states they built.<br /> <br /> This was lost in the new versions. Hazlan wasn't about magic, it was about racism, with a racist tyrant focused on Nazi-style research and a pogrom for genocide, curiously against his own politically dominant ethnicity. Drakov was at once Tepes and Ivan, but also Hitler, Stalin and Pol Pot.<br /> <br /> Heck, they even removed his branding of the peoples of Falkovnia, now it is just a tattoo the loyal troops make somewhere in their bodies. Yeah, I know branding people like cattle isn't a good thing to do. That's why it was a villain doing that, one almost devoid of redeeming qualities.<br /> <br /> But on another note, I'm not sure if the current model is working. I have already the text on I'Cath done and am ready to write Kalakeri and Kartakass. But is this model of commenting each Domain with my usual verborragic length working?<br /> <br /> What do you say?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly the way you're going is a solid way to get through the book. Considering the effort put into presenting these domains in book, tackling them individually to decide on what worked and didn't is a good approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T16:44:07-08:00","id":1469676,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Har'Akir might've worked better if it'd decided to lean in more to the original Mummy film, where the titular character isn't the bandaged form he often got associated with outside of a few minutes in the opening, and is instead this mysterious creepy old man lurking about modern Cairo.<br /> Maybe a pre-18th century Egyptian style city alongside a haunted river that runs through a malevolent desert (sandstorms standing in for the Mists), and Anhktepot can mostly pass for one of the living (even though he's really tall and has weathered skin, sunken eyes, and a very intimidating aura), but while he rules his hidden collection of cultists, setting-appropriate undead, and other creatures with an iron hand, any attempt to actually take control of the city-state's throne and become the great king he believes he should be results in total failure and often forcing him back into slumber for a period in order to recover his power. Then you have this entire thing of palace intrigue and politics for the PCs to get entangled with, as well as all the usual shenanigans of back alley crime, scheming merchants, murder mysteries, trying to uncover lost artifacts from the desert, and what not. <br /> And if you're keeping the concept of the Amber Wastes, then the above mentioned haunted river can eventually lead toward other domains, including Tiyet's wealthy yet hauntingly quiet estate of Sebua, the Emirate-like realm of Pharazia, and perhaps even eventually to the now empty Ashen Wastes that were once Cavitius, or to the Wildlands if one wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T12:22:11-08:00","id":1469758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469670#post1469670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would make sense and it is probably the reason behind some changes in it and in other domains, but for Har'Akir it doesn't actually add up.<br /> <br /> Again, the problem is that they <i>outright say it was the Egyptian Pantheon</i>. It is in a side box in the domain's write-up. Ankhtepot was a priest of the Egyptian Pantheon and the Akiri worshiped the Egyptian Pantheon when the domain formed.<br /> <br /> Instead of avoiding this particular stereotype, they double down on it. And the new Akiri Pantheon isn't worked as a fantasy religion, but outright as a fake religion. And the lost temples of the Egyptian Pantheon are still there to be discovered by adventurers.<br /> <br /> So while they certainly developed Har'Akir beyond just being Egypt as seen by the British, it is still pretty much Egypt. And it actually has more mummies than original Har'Akir.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers of the Domain have mentioned that it is meant to &quot;gaslight&quot; the players, to make them say &quot;it doesn't make sense- or is it?&quot; and overall confuse them. Now, I am not saying they did a good job with it- in fact, I agree that the execution is dubious saying the least- but that is the logic behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T14:33:24-08:00","id":1469765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469758#post1469758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers of the Domain have mentioned that it is meant to &quot;gaslight&quot; the players, to make them say &quot;it doesn't make sense- or is it?&quot; and overall confuse them. Now, I am not saying they did a good job with it- in fact, I agree that the execution is dubious saying the least- but that is the logic behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see where the authors gave interview, I'm really curious about all of them. And while I believe the amount of change was probably a top-down command, I would like to know their reasoning on their decisions for execution.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the next batch of domains is here.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>I\u2019CATH</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">This was a seriously unexpected entry. Even counting every use in supplements, novels and adventure modules, I\u2019Cath has only been published twice, in the first Islands of Terror of 1992 and in the 1997\u2019s Domains of Dread.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On the other hand, we can pretty much say it still stands, because this iteration is the same only in name. Even Hazlan seems more akin to the original, almost nothing from previous I\u2019Cath was kept, just few names and the Palace of Bones. Everything that made Tsien Chiang tick as Dark Lord was stripped from her and replaced.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Which is actually good, because I\u2019Cath was horrible. I\u2019Cath was basically a roofless dungeon with a linear plot and no people to meaningfully interact, even Nightingale was too shallow and had a simple role in putting the adventurers on the top of her tower, otherwise it was like a dumb re-enact of Legend of Zelda with less palaces. Tsien Chiang had a wonderful premise as a powerful evil lord and wizard before it was common to give such roles to women without caveats, but it was wasted with nonsensical misandry (she did had a reason to start, but it didn\u2019t actually went anywhere or did anything aside being repeated ad nauseum) and generally being evil for the sake of it in an extremely cartoonish way. She was like a combination of Cruella DeVil and Maleficent, but distilled of any interesting quality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">New I\u2019Cath combines several almost-abandoned old domain concepts into a new, cohesive whole. It is a bit of the Nightmare Lands (just a bit), a lot of old Timor (especially the background before the Marikit Queen) and, of course, some I\u2019Cath (actually less than Timor), along with the more-than-once used trope of despair against possible starvation (strong, but not extreme as in G\u2019Henna).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">As a whole the domain is well written and the dual aspect of ream and reality works well, with good rules on how to navigate them. The new daughters of Tsien Chiang (the only thing that still significantly numbers four) are simple (by design) but interesting. I only miss better illustrations, both the daughters and the dream-city streets begged for visualization in place of the Jiangshi attack. The city also have several factions that can be approached in more than one way, with the Adventure hooks including a Jiangshi as quest giver, a nice touch.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Chiang is well written, but as other in the book her new backstory is maybe too much sympathetic. It is hard to see her as the same level of evil as Strahd or Azalin, as she not only have a good start, but actually many good intentions without so much of a falling arc that entirely justifies her predicament. She seems more delirious than really evil, vengeful streak aside. I miss some aspects of old Tsien Chiang a little, especially her obsession with the number four, but all in all, good riddance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">My only real criticism and parting thought is that more than a hint of the old one-tone of I\u2019Cath was maintained. The write-up is pretty explicit that whatever adventures you run on I\u2019Cath, the party will have to disturb Tsien Chiang\u2019s Dream City to escape I\u2019Cath, and little is given as adventure material outside setting to that as greater goal. It isn\u2019t impossible to use I\u2019Cath in other ways, but the book won\u2019t help you.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>KALAKERI</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Here we have a domain that changed even the name! But I must say it makes perfectly sense. The problem with the old name Sri Raji is that it is, actually, the Hindi equivalent of naming your domain \u201cMister President\u201d. So they found a compromise in changing the name to Kalakeri, then in the text saying that outsiders gave it several other names through the ages, including \u201cSri Raji\u201d. A clever solution to a stupid problem. From now on on this text I\u2019ll use Sri Raji when talking about the old domain and Kalakeri when talking about the new version.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Now, Sri Raji was a special case in old Ravenloft, in the sense that it was the worse offender in being a British stereotype of a non-European culture, as if it came directly from a 19</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> century Gothic Horror book written in London. It had zero traits that didn\u2019t boil down to that standard racist description of India. While I\u2019m against the way they choose to change things by unannounced retcon, I have to agree that changing this domain was a necessity. I\u2019m not so sure about Arijani\u2019s background, though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Simply put, the history of the three Vasadavan siblings fight over the land is good, but making Ramya the Darklord doesn\u2019t work so well. She\u2019s mad, but she <b>is</b> the wronged party and the lesser evil of the three all things considered. She\u2019s an interesting character and definitely need to be put down to rest, but she just don\u2019t make the cut for Darklord, much less under the shadow of the guy who made Rakshasas seem like decent citizens. It is evidently worse with the new version of Arijani, albeit strange, being still a worse person and cut for Darklord, maybe in conjunction with Inajira (I\u2019m not sure of what to make of this new version of Inajira, but since they changed Strahd\u2019s pact, lets put it to rest for now).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Aside the Darklord identity, Kalakeri works remarkably well. The trio of villains and their constant conflict make for a great background for any number of adventures without need to make them the actual focus, despite still having a strong impact. The use they make of the Renown system is simple but very good, giving GM and PCs alike the tools to figure out how to manage their relation with the two warring factions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><b>KARTAKASS</b></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">They kicked up a notch the whole concept of \u201cdomain of music\u201d here. Where Kartakass used to be a collection of quaint villages in the woods, now it is Big Time Show Business! I\u2019m not sure of how much it works as domain, but it surely is unique. Even the beasts and trees are artists here, and the horror comes from the ugly parts of the entertainment industry. And werewolves, of course.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On one hand, small villages and folk music are far more my thing, so I can\u2019t say a lot about the change myself. On the other hand we have more settlements and an easy method for thinking up more and giving them unique feels. The domain have lots of opportunities for adventure without involving the Darklord and tracking reputation as celebrities is an interesting change of pace, but the single note of it may become tiring after a time and it isn\u2019t so refreshing right after another, more complex take on the reputation system.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">No more is Harkon Lukas a Wolfwere. This is a disappointment for me, that liked the finer details that made him and his domain different from lycanthropes. But then, this is such a fine detail that it may well be unnecessary baggage for some, who am I to say? Now this is a domain of both standard and slightly stronger Werewolves, and Lukas curses people with Lycanthropy on purpose. Changing back probably wouldn\u2019t be a big deal, though, just re-purposing the werewolf statistics.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It makes more of a difference on the characters presented. Harkon itself underwent less changes than many other Darklords, the biggest one being that instead of detached due to living in a rural area nor worth of his ambitions, now he\u2019s fully engaged with it and yet is cursed to be forgotten in short notice, buried beneath the sheer amount of new artists. His backstory had a few tweaks to be simplified, which I thought unnecessary, but the base is the same.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Greater difference is in his children, for anyone who cares. Akriel and Casimir Lukas are back and have some role in the domain, even if minor. They are human now, and work more like references to their previous versions than filling the same roles in the story. Still, they can be used for a range of purposes, so it isn\u2019t a big loss.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Next time we'll have Lamordia, and a huge lot of rant, then Mordent, the first I just skipped because I decided to write this review, so it will be a complete surprise, hence I'm not promising to do Richemulot in the same batch.<br /> <br /> With this we're getting near to the final run of domains. Tepest and Valachan I had an <i>en passant</i> reading and at least they seem to follow through their plot more than retcon them, keeping the legacy of the old Darklords. After that, a collection of old and new domains in brief descriptions, and we finally move to other parts of the book. Maybe the beginning, maybe the end, I'm open to suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T15:57:35-08:00","id":1469776,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/22417339/van-richtens-guide-to-ravenloft-harakir-ankhotep-the-mummy-preview\" target=\"_blank\">Here </a>is the link for the Har'Akir's preview interview, explaining at least some of their reasoning for the changes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T17:00:20-08:00","id":1469787,"title":"","content":"Regarding I'Cath, I think it was one of those prime examples of the biggest problem with early Ravenloft, especially the Islands of Terror, where too many domains were essentially just elaborate dungeons the PCs would wander into randomly and then have little to do there outside the designed adventure. This is one of the reasons I enjoyed the addition of the Clusters, so that some of them could be expanded into something closer to a functioning society. <br /> Although, the Verdurous Land/Steaming Land wasn't a very good one, as the only real commonality between Saragossa, Sri Raji, and the Wildlands is that they are hot and humid. In hindsight, I think Sri Raji might've worked OK if attached to the Core as a little Sri Lankan-like island in the Nocturnal Sea. (This would come with the idea that the realm should almost explicitly be the dark equivalent of Ravana and his island fortress of Lanka from Ramayana.) The Saragossa I'd likely make the warmer southern extension of the Sea of Sorrows, with Souragne as an island on its edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T06:26:04-08:00","id":1469828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469776#post1469776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.polygon.com/22417339/van-richtens-guide-to-ravenloft-harakir-ankhotep-the-mummy-preview\" target=\"_blank\">Here </a>is the link for the Har'Akir's preview interview, explaining at least some of their reasoning for the changes</div> </div> </div> </div>That was interesting, and explains some things. Yet, it still offends me as a fan.<br /> <br /> Ravenloft <b>is</b> plagued by a lot of derivative work and racist stereotypes. But retconing the entire setting doesn't necessarily solves nothing, and isn't really needed to solve things.<br /> <br /> Time and new editions had already done a lot of work towards making things better. Clusters especially, along with Mistways, do a lot for adding twists and complexities to the domains, as those distinct derivations have to interact with other realities.<br /> <br /> And making things more high fantasy? D&amp;D isn't just high fantasy and this is one of the things that I actively don't like in the game, to have to be high fantasy. I like the interaction between high and low. I like grounded settings and concepts to start with. I prefer high fantasy when it is an irregular addition instead of the default to be expected.<br /> <br /> When everything is special, nothing is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T16:54:29-08:00","id":1469883,"title":"","content":"I was always a little disappointed that they never tried a Ravenloft setting for d20 Modern. I think you could've done something interesting with some sort of Gotham-esque city surrounded by industrial wastelands, creepily quiet suburbs, haunted highways, abandoned summer camps, and strange theme parks. But I'm weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T18:32:38-08:00","id":1469887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469883#post1469883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always a little disappointed that they never tried a Ravenloft setting for d20 Modern. I think you could've done something interesting with some sort of Gotham-esque city surrounded by industrial wastelands, creepily quiet suburbs, haunted highways, abandoned summer camps, and strange theme parks. But I'm weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seemed to be what 2nd edition AD&amp;D was leading up towards. We got the Ravenloft &quot;Masque of the Red Death&quot; setting, which was basically a slightly alternate version of Earth in the 1890-1900 timeframe, with an equal parts mix of history, conspiracy and horror. I remember way back on usenet one of the authors mentioned that there was discussion in TSR and work being done for a new modern-horror setting, probably due to seeing how successful Vampire: the Masquerade was, but then TSR got bought out by WotC the next year and that was the end of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T19:04:25-08:00","id":1469890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469828#post1469828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was interesting, and explains some things. Yet, it still offends me as a fan.<br /> <br /> Ravenloft <b>is</b> plagued by a lot of derivative work and racist stereotypes. But retconing the entire setting doesn't necessarily solves nothing, and isn't really needed to solve things.<br /> <br /> Time and new editions had already done a lot of work towards making things better. Clusters especially, along with Mistways, do a lot for adding twists and complexities to the domains, as those distinct derivations have to interact with other realities.<br /> <br /> And making things more high fantasy? D&amp;D isn't just high fantasy and this is one of the things that I actively don't like in the game, to have to be high fantasy. I like the interaction between high and low. I like grounded settings and concepts to start with. I prefer high fantasy when it is an irregular addition instead of the default to be expected.<br /> <br /> When everything is special, nothing is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That article made me claw at my face a bit as far as my issues with the whole soulless construct citizens of Ravenloft, I'm going to be honest.<br /> <br /> &quot;We want people to feel like the people of the domains have their own agency and internally valid culture and are not just a battleground for adventures by outsiders. But also, we're going to stress that the majority of the people of Ravenloft are soulless p-zombies with no agency. Also, the domains are going to all be barely connected floating pocket dimensions within the Shadowfell, not even within a single demiplane, and the more usual references are going to be to them as places that the mists yank you into.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are good things in that hardcover, but they largely just make the bad things that much more exasperating. And knowing the reasoning behind some of them makes me want to cry out as to why the developers could not just pick a lane, as it were.<br /> <br /> edit: This particularly, as far as an actual quote<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">This can very easily be [a story about] your home. [Your character] can imagine a world where there are not these horrors, and it\u2019s up to you to make them better.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We have straight up published an adventure that states the domain will just reset to factory settings eventually if Strahd is killed. We've also said in this book that is a regular thing that happens with domains if you take out the darklord.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd be all over the idea that people of a domain could achieve some measure of heroism, rise to the challenges before them, and through some campaign of harrowing and terrifying adventures manage to overcome the darklord of the land. That's great. That's the stuff of adventures. That's a solid compromise between D&amp;D and Horror as it were, which is the line Ravenloft has always had to tread.<br /> <br /> If Van Richten's is wanting to send that message, it is telling it in the most muddled, self undermining and self contradictory way it could have chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 12-07-2021, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T19:11:00-08:00","id":1469891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469887#post1469887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seemed to be what 2nd edition AD&amp;D was leading up towards. We got the Ravenloft &quot;Masque of the Red Death&quot; setting, which was basically a slightly alternate version of Earth in the 1890-1900 timeframe, with an equal parts mix of history, conspiracy and horror. I remember way back on usenet one of the authors mentioned that there was discussion in TSR and work being done for a new modern-horror setting, probably due to seeing how successful Vampire: the Masquerade was, but then TSR got bought out by WotC the next year and that was the end of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that may have been the Dark Matter setting for Alternity. Which was a really cool setting, but not quite the same thing. <br /> <br /> I think in my mind I have this idea of a generic &quot;every city&quot; (in my case, North American, but it could manifest as anything), where every urban horror story, real or imagined, you've ever heard likely takes place. Giant man eating alligators in the sewer system. Ghost trains in the subways. Serial killers. Dangerous gang lords. People above the law. Murder hotels. Lost 13th floors of buildings. Apartments full of Satanic cultists. Undead being kept alive by refrigeration. Vampires. Haunted mansions. Mad science experiments at the university. Maniac cops. All of it. The suburbs around it are full of ghosts, dream-haunting killers, teen witches, Stepford Wives, rabid dogs, and murder clowns. Even the roads and highways are full of vanishing hitchhikers, killer cars, and haunted roadside bars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T21:18:56-08:00","id":1469897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469891#post1469891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that may have been the Dark Matter setting for Alternity. Which was a really cool setting, but not quite the same thing.<br /> <br /> I think in my mind I have this idea of a generic &quot;every city&quot; (in my case, North American, but it could manifest as anything), where every urban horror story, real or imagined, you've ever heard likely takes place. Giant man eating alligators in the sewer system. Ghost trains in the subways. Serial killers. Dangerous gang lords. People above the law. Murder hotels. Lost 13th floors of buildings. Apartments full of Satanic cultists. Undead being kept alive by refrigeration. Vampires. Haunted mansions. Mad science experiments at the university. Maniac cops. All of it. The suburbs around it are full of ghosts, dream-haunting killers, teen witches, Stepford Wives, rabid dogs, and murder clowns. Even the roads and highways are full of vanishing hitchhikers, killer cars, and haunted roadside bars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really like this concept. A 5e Modern campaign set in an urban horror Domain of Dread.<br /> <br /> As I thought about it, an extra complication to the concept crept into my head: that of a veneer of normalcy.<br /> <br /> The concept is that the inhabitants - who, as is the case with other Domains, are soulless constructs - are on at least some level aware that something is very wrong with their world. But they're both ignorant and incurious, and will latch onto any non-supernatural explanation of events. They don't believe in monsters and don't want to. Except they still kind of do, they just don't want to admit it. The inhabitants vacillate between superstitious paranoia and dogmatic skepticism, depending on which way the wind is blowing.<br /> <br /> This is to the benefit of the monsters that secretly control the Domain, who may or may not be the Darklord and their agents. Like Vampire: The Masquerade, a screen of secrecy, misinformation, and cover-ups serves to maintain the illusion that everything is fine. That there are no monsters, no magic, and certainly no predators preying on the citizens. A fiction said citizens cling to, in between bouts of spreading rumors of monsters and occasionally being whipped up into paranoid mobs.<br /> <br /> The PCs in such a campaign might be contacted very early on by agents of the Darklord, informing them in no uncertain terms that they'll be allowed to deal with the random monsters, serial killers, and evil cults they encounter. They might even enjoy strings being pulled to keep them out of trouble with the law (who are, of course, horribly corrupt and partially stocked with monsters themselves; so, no change there). With the caveat that the PCs need to stay quiet about it all, or they'll be crushed, either by assassins or by the systems that bend to the Darklord's whims. While the party is free - encouraged, even - to clean up small evils in the margins of society, they cannot be permitted to tackle the rot at the center of it.<br /> <br /> At least, not until the PCs become high enough level that they can start fighting back.<br /> <br /> The very first idea I had when I thought of this conceit was that of a Scooby Doo style band of teen sleuths and their intelligent animal mascot, who go around solving mysteries. To muddie the waters, the Domain would be filled with perfectly mundane criminals who dress up as monsters, to accomplish some mundane crime. The Scoobies go around foiling their plans, gaining notoriety for their efforts. Though they don't know it, they serve the interests of the Powers That Be/Darklord, by reinforcing the idea that everything that seems supernatural has a mundane explanation. The teens, for their part, are unaware of this, being largely benign in and of themselves. While some of their number are credulous enough to entertain the idea of monsters in the moment, they're ultimately confident, from experience, that monsters aren't real. The masks always come off in the end.<br /> <br /> Which can lead to the amusing situation where the PCs need to follow the sleuths around, protecting them from real monsters. All while being pressured into not enlightening the sleuths, even if the party have ample evidence of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T04:57:54-08:00","id":1469906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469883#post1469883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. I entertained the idea of modern and even futuristic Domains since the first time I read Ravenloft. I've did it once, although the game didn't last long enough to reach there, for real life reasons (my personal fall out with one of the players), but it was fun to run a bunch of Technocrats with a wrecked Union spaceship lost in the woods of Forlorn.<br /> <br /> I thoroughly encourage my players into bring characters from <i>any</i> game into Ravenloft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469890#post1469890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That article made me claw at my face a bit as far as my issues with the whole soulless construct citizens of Ravenloft, I'm going to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The article is interesting because of the things it shows underneath of the workings behind the whole process. It also explains Har'Akir well enough.<br /> <br /> But given all the contradictions between the article and the rest of the book, it also shows how fragmented the work was, so that the team working on Har'Akir labored under complete different assumptions from other teams.<br /> <br /> Also, that many artists had no love or previous knowledge of the setting, as pretty much 3/4 or more of what they said they aimed to accomplish is just 3rd edition Ravenloft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469897#post1469897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I thought about it, an extra complication to the concept crept into my head: that of a veneer of normalcy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if this must be focused for a Ravenloft Domain, at least not in such Masquerade-like way.<br /> <br /> People fearing the things-that-go-bump-in-the-night but choosing to shut up about this is very Ravenloft. People being magically made unaware by the Mists too. But a concerted effort to keep this by the monstrous denizens, not so much.<br /> <br /> Especially, though, we must think about the Darklord. Remember that the Darklord in Ravenloft isn't necessarily a ruler, but is necessarily a prisoner, a cursed one on top of that. Although the Domain must be open to adventures unrelated to them, it <b>does</b> exist in function of the Darklord.<br /> <br /> Who's this tortured soul? How they get the attention of the Dark Powers, and how they are tormented by the Domain? Lets think about that and how it may create an unique relationship between setting and villain, before just setting course to make &quot;VtM for D&amp;D&quot;.<br /> <br /> On another note, as of late I'm not feeling very well and it may take some time before we explore Lamordia and Mordent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T09:08:53-08:00","id":1469921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469906#post1469906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, that many artists had no love or previous knowledge of the setting, as pretty much 3/4 or more of what they said they aimed to accomplish is just 3rd edition Ravenloft.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is a key point all across the book. I am not sure that the writing team has even gave a look at 3e Ravenloft. In some cases, it feels like they tried avoiding it like from fire- like how they threw Sithicus away because &quot;Lord Soth is no longer in Ravenloft&quot; while ignoring how events went on in the novels (which have actually predated the 3e Ravenloft line). I am not going to say that they did not did any research, but in many cases it feels like they did a very minimal one or just ignored it in order to bring their own vision for Ravenloft without caring about previous lore. As a point, Cawford has stated that the novels and previous lore are not considered canon anymore as far as official material is concerned, which is, like, very annoying for someone who actually like the setting. There is a reason that the main Ravenloft facebook group publish its own material through the DMGuild- while most didn't gone &quot;fanrage&quot; over it (which is nice for a change) and many have tried to reconstruct a path between old Ravenloft and new Ravenloft, it seems like most felt disappointed from the path that WotC took. From what it looked like, people were ok with having changes for the setting, but they wanted it to evolve, not to have retcones or hear that their favorite material is &quot;non canon&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T18:02:50-08:00","id":1469984,"title":"","content":"Ravenloft in 5th edition feels a bit like the Forgotten Realms in 4th edition. They basically hit the reset button on Ravenloft, dramatically altered the setting in fundamental ways in order to fit a new vision and so that the setting was more friendly to new players who had little to no experience with the setting, but at the cost of tossing out a lot of stuff that long time older players had enjoyed about the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T20:10:25-08:00","id":1469996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469906#post1469906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On another note, as of late I'm not feeling very well and it may take some time before we explore Lamordia and Mordent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best wishes for feeling better. <br /> <br /> I suspect the ultimate Darklord for my theoretical modern urban setting would end up drawing a lot of inspiration from Fredersen and Rotwang in Metropolis, with additional elements from Dark City, 1984, Alan Moore's V for Vendetta, and Watchmen mixed in. Then there'd be a bunch of smaller domains within it and around it. <br /> <br /> I had a thought that if one wanted to have the original Ravenloft and its Core &quot;evolve&quot; into the mass of disconnected realms in the Shadow Plane, one way would be to have Gwydion (Darklord of the Shadow Rift) finally tear its way out of the Obsidian Gate and end up shattering the Core, perhaps alongside something which frees Ebonbane from its sword form and other cataclysmic events. But I like the Core, so would be unlikely to do such a thing myself. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T08:36:22-08:00","id":1470035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469984#post1469984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravenloft in 5th edition feels a bit like the Forgotten Realms in 4th edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a lot like that, but I do suspect something more insidious behind it. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> said, they seemed to very specifically avoid or ignore 3rd edition material, focusing on mentions and references to 2nd edition every time.<br /> <br /> Third edition wasn't done in-house. It was by Arthaus/White Wolf. They seem keen on deconstructing whatever was accomplished in it, even more than any other edition. They seem to be targeting to harm 3rd edition on purpose.<br /> <br /> Is there still some IP shenanigans over the matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1469996#post1469996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a thought that if one wanted to have the original Ravenloft and its Core &quot;evolve&quot; into the mass of disconnected realms in the Shadow Plane, one way would be to have Gwydion (Darklord of the Shadow Rift) finally tear its way out of the Obsidian Gate and end up shattering the Core, perhaps alongside something which frees Ebonbane from its sword form and other cataclysmic events. But I like the Core, so would be unlikely to do such a thing myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>One advantage of Ravenloft metaphysics is that incorporating and reverting the new material isn't unfeasible.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the Ravenloft Gazetteers were designed to end up in another of Azalin's megalomaniac plots (&quot;S&quot; was one of his clones, and her journey was designed to set up the events for this new thing), one that could cause widespread changes to the setting.<br /> <br /> You know, like they did in the Grand Conjunction.<br /> <br /> It isn't too hard to have new Darkon resolve with Azalin's comeback and the return of the Core, collapsing the new Domains with their old counterparts, maybe explaining where the old versions were to keep continuity, then keeping in place the good changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T17:21:28-08:00","id":1470090,"title":"","content":"Some of this may be a side effect of WOTC being owned by Hasbro. Hasbro apparently has some sort of unspoken corporate policy of not allowing fans of various properties to actually be involved with them. This has resulted in some missteps over the past couple of years, culminating in the recent failure of their HasLab crowdfunding of a Rancor Monster for the Star Wars Black Series line. I have no idea how much this mentality is at play in WOTC, or if it had any impact on who was chosen to work on 5E Ravenloft or how they decided what to do with existing material, but it's always a possibility. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T13:28:18-08:00","id":1470294,"title":"","content":"My computer kinda died last Thursday because of a blackout, only got to put it up and running again one hour ago or so. I'm tired, but if not today, I'll try to make the next step tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T11:40:00-08:00","id":1470360,"title":"","content":"I was looking at the original boxed set this weekend, and it occurred to me that Arak was a very weird choice for a domain. Mainly because it was just sort of there doing absolutely nothing. The original book gave little to no information about it, no one lives there (anymore, not since the creation of Keening destroyed its surface), and nothing really happens there, baring anyone spending the night getting taken away by the mysterious underground &quot;elves&quot;. I get the feeling that there might've been this idea of having an adventure module set in Arak that was eventually going to detail the domain and explain the inhabitants, which I presume were originally intended to be something similar to the Drow. (I'm not sure if it would've been the Shadow Fey we eventually got.) But in a way, I kind of feel like this was a missed opportunity to give Ravenloft a dwarven domain, perhaps based on Tolkien's works (either the Hobbit idea of a dwarf king consumed by greed or the LotR's mines full of ghosts and tormented by a demonic monster they dug up). Perhaps with the realm of the the shadow fey and Gwydion the Sorcerer-Fiend being below it as part of Ravenloft's answer to the Underdark. (Maybe alongside Bleutspur and the God-Brain.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T13:42:15-08:00","id":1470367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470360#post1470360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking at the original boxed set this weekend, and it occurred to me that Arak was a very weird choice for a domain. Mainly because it was just sort of there doing absolutely nothing. The original book gave little to no information about it, no one lives there (anymore, not since the creation of Keening destroyed its surface), and nothing really happens there, baring anyone spending the night getting taken away by the mysterious underground &quot;elves&quot;. I get the feeling that there might've been this idea of having an adventure module set in Arak that was eventually going to detail the domain and explain the inhabitants, which I presume were originally intended to be something similar to the Drow. (I'm not sure if it would've been the Shadow Fey we eventually got.) But in a way, I kind of feel like this was a missed opportunity to give Ravenloft a dwarven domain, perhaps based on Tolkien's works (either the Hobbit idea of a dwarf king consumed by greed or the LotR's mines full of ghosts and tormented by a demonic monster they dug up). Perhaps with the realm of the the shadow fey and Gwydion the Sorcerer-Fiend being below it as part of Ravenloft's answer to the Underdark. (Maybe alongside Bleutspur and the God-Brain.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting, as they already had an Elvish domain. But in the end they set up for the Shadow Fey, which I think worked as the seed for the whole idea of the Shadowfell.<br /> <br /> Before continuing I must say, the maps on this book are really something. Loved them even when I hated the domain, that much I must confess. I wish we had something like this in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>LAMORDIA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I seriously don\u2019t like what they did here. It could work as a new domain entirely, but even then I\u2019m not sure. This is too Grimdark and stripped the stories it purposes to tell from their needed context. It may work for body horror for sure, but definitely not for the Gothic tale of the Created.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Lamordia was not a land about the maladies of science and industry as it is now. Quite the contrary, it was about the goodness in science and industry. Why? Because that backdrop makes the contrast needed for the tales of wicked science to work. When everyone is required by necessity to be unethical you don\u2019t have horror about science, you have horror about the system.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">And new Lamordia is horror about the system in spades, an extremely on the nose criticism on capitalism with a strong take on the tales of the Robber Barons of 19</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> century England, Nazi German and a lot of Atomic Fear. It really doesn\u2019t gel here, despite being good fodder for a Domain for certain. As is now, it robs all the drama from the tales of hidden blasphemies by mad doctors and instead seems like a Black Dog supplement about Pentex.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">For the Darklord, as above so below. They changed almost everything in Mordenheim\u2019s background, mostly for the worse. But lets tackle the elephant in the room first and foremost: <b>Mordenheim as a lesbian woman isn\u2019t in the least a problem</b>. The story works perfectly well with this, even the original tale would, as Victor and Elise never had biological children anyways. If the lack of children was due to infertility, lack of sex, or them being just a homosexual couple is immaterial, as it was never deemed a source of drama on itself anyway.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But changing Elise to a petty criminal when making them lesbians? <b>That\u2019s some messed up coding</b>. All the drama from the original story was stripped for this shitty arrangement. It is a love story between criminals that end badly because of the creation of a McGuffing, not because of obsession, loneliness or alienation. And now Elise\u2019s exile is just because there\u2019s no honor among thieves. Wait, wasn\u2019t Viktra so obsessed for her that she managed to create the McGuffing in the first place? Whatever, now she just wants the Thing, Elise be damned.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On the Von Aubrecker front, things got butchered again. Replacing the Baron for his son Rudolph-Brain-in-a-Jar was a bad but expected development. Nothing terrible about that that aren\u2019t already covered by the first three paragraphs above. But turning Gerta from actual power behind her father to a mere dominated butler? Why?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The more I look at NuLamordia, the more I despise this write-up. Looking at the whole picture, what seems as a diversity-friendly domain at least in the gender/sex area is actually a lot of disguised prejudice. Lesbians with no redeeming quality, women are there to serve, modern society is endangered but the mutants running amok due to its own modern failings. Gods, how I hate this write-up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Well, it does have a few good things about it. The adventure ideas are good enough and are really diverse. The advice on running a game for characters experimented upon by Viktra are good, although the lack of mechanics to help the process really harms the intended goal (just use another stat block isn\u2019t a good mechanic for PCs). And the Serving Dr. Mordenheim table is short but does its job.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">My final note, so: they wasted more than four pages with a messed up domain that doesn\u2019t work for its intended purpose and an offensive excuse for a villain that doesn\u2019t justify anything about the place, then used just about one and a half page for the really good stuff, that suffered greatly for getting so little.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>MORDENT</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Simply put, while Barovia is the most iconic Ravenloft domain, Mordent is its vanilla and always has been. It is the easiest domain to make a classic horror tale, it is already very similar to the English countryside that is kind of a staple of the classic Gothic, it has a social structure that is rigid, but not overwhelmingly so and is easy to understand and use. It is the home of the Van Richten\u2019s Herbalist Shop, and of many scholar societies studying the demiplane as a whole. In a sense, it is the heart of the setting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On the other hand two big problems plague Mordent as a setting, derived from its origins. First a counterpoint to being vanilla, it lacks a stronger flavor. It is hard to point a unifying theme to it outside \u201cthere be ghosts\u201d. Is hard to hear a tale and say \u201cthat could only happen in Mordent\u201d, unless it relied too much on very specific characters, of course. The other problem is that Godefroy has never been very interesting as a Darklord.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Both problems have a common origin in the nature of the original module <i>Ravenloft 2: The House on Gryphon Hill</i>. Basically speaking, <i>Ravenloft 2</i> was built around a single event that would come to a resolution at the end one way or another, so almost nothing on it can meaningfully endure in the setting, and the story\u2019s villains are better used elsewhere (Strahd and Azalin).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">That means Godefroy was designed for the Domain and not the opposite, and was a simple design. A Darklord that is a ghost, so the haunting on Gryphon Hill remains iconic. And that\u2019s it! Godefroy\u2019s evil isn\u2019t spectacular, or far reaching, you get by his story that even the Mist seem to only care about Mordent to take the Apparatus and the Alchemist, and Godefroy was made Darklord just because it should have one. For many years he remained the single most isolated Darklord with such a large Domain, and even after they made him a kind of ghost mob boss he felt without a purpose.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">My criticism on old Godefroy is important to frame what changed about Mordent here. This is by far the most intact domain in relation to previous material, to begin with, and I liked the changes. Mordent retains most of its features and themes, but they\u2019re more sharp, lets say. A local curse to make everyone into a ghost also helps to make it feel special without changing much in the overall nature of the domain, although it may be a bit too far if taken to a broader setting, but that\u2019s minor. Rudolph Van Richten still being alive is another matter, for another moment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Lord Godefroy, though, had just a bit more of tweaks that made for a far greater role in the whole domain, and finally gave him what it takes to be the Darklord for real, instead of just a glorified haunt. Linking him to the story of the Apparatus puts him in the center of the events, and now his actions go far enough to add some thousand deaths under his belt. His personality is better defined and yet the same, and now he actually does have a plan, a greater purpose to direct his actions as the ghostly mob boss he still is.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Closing the write-up, the adventure ideas and advice on making ghost-story adventures aren\u2019t brilliant, but are passable and close well what is otherwise an almost flawless write-up, and we part ways with an art of how the Ghost Mob looks like that is almost as good as Strahd\u2019s is bad. Up to now, this is my favorite domain art, close to Vladeska\u2019s battle and some points above Saidra\u2019s Masquerade. Others are beautiful, but those are the best at capturing the feel and themes of the domain and its Darklord.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T13:46:48-08:00","id":1470369,"title":"","content":"Next time is Richemulot, Tepest and Valachan. The first I'm yet to read, the last two have legacy Darklords, finally, a concept previously brushed aside even when the original domain had it. Then our last look at the domains will go to the Others, a collection of single-paragraph quick write-ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T14:17:29-08:00","id":1470375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470369#post1470369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next time is Richemulot, Tepest and Valachan. The first I'm yet to read, the last two have legacy Darklords, finally, a concept previously brushed aside even when the original domain had it. Then our last look at the domains will go to the Others, a collection of single-paragraph quick write-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just wanted to note I'm continuing to enjoy and appreciate the review. You're voicing a variety of the things I liked and disliked about Ravenloft 5e in an interesting and nuanced way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T17:51:22-08:00","id":1470400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470367#post1470367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">For the Darklord, as above so below. They changed almost everything in Mordenheim\u2019s background, mostly for the worse. But lets tackle the elephant in the room first and foremost: <b>Mordenheim as a lesbian woman isn\u2019t in the least a problem</b>. The story works perfectly well with this, even the original tale would, as Victor and Elise never had biological children anyways. If the lack of children was due to infertility, lack of sex, or them being just a homosexual couple is immaterial, as it was never deemed a source of drama on itself anyway.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just to double check is Mordenheim the Darklord now? Because in the previous editions it was always Adam who was the Darklord of Lamordia. That's a pretty massive alteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T19:10:16-08:00","id":1470403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470400#post1470400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/FONT][/COLOR][/COLOR]Just to double check is Mordenheim the Darklord now? Because in the previous editions it was always Adam who was the Darklord of Lamordia. That's a pretty massive alteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is.<br /> <br /> Mordenheim is the Darklord and Adam doesn't exist. Instead they mashed-up Adam and Elise. She was successfully resurrected with the Unbreakable Heart, which stands for the actual Creation this time, and she uses Flesh Golem stats just 'cause. Viktra is the Darklord, but Elise is on the run because she believes her lover who created a miraculous heart made of gold to save her life will now just kill her to take the thing back.<br /> <br /> And apparently she will, because she can't recreate the damn thing and now it is more important. Because reasons. It's not like Viktra is free only because the Mists took her while she was being arrested for the crimes she committed to save Elise's life. Crimes she knew to be risky because she she wasn't used to do those things herself, but she had to save her lover that was also her personal professional grave-robber.<br /> <br /> The placement of Adam as the Darklord had a reason, as Mordenheim himself was indifferent to his own predicament. Lamordia does <b>not</b> torment Mordenheim, not before and not now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T20:15:46-08:00","id":1470406,"title":"","content":"That all sounds pretty... awkward. It's a shame, Mordenheim and his relationship with Adam was always one of the things I found the most interesting when it came to Ravenloft's setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T22:20:38-08:00","id":1470410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470367#post1470367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lamordia was not a land about the maladies of science and industry as it is now. Quite the contrary, it was about the goodness in science and industry. Why? Because that backdrop makes the contrast needed for the tales of wicked science to work. When everyone is required by necessity to be unethical you don\u2019t have horror about science, you have horror about the system.<br /> And new Lamordia is horror about the system in spades, an extremely on the nose criticism on capitalism with a strong take on the tales of the Robber Barons of 19th century England, Nazi German and a lot of Atomic Fear. It really doesn\u2019t gel here, despite being good fodder for a Domain for certain. As is now, it robs all the drama from the tales of hidden blasphemies by mad doctors and instead seems like a Black Dog supplement about Pentex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't there an Island of Terror domain specifically made for the &quot;horrors of the Industrial Revolution and pollution&quot; theme? I'm totally blanking on the name, but I know I remember it from somewhere.<br /> <br /> As for Lamordia, part of the impression I always had of it was a land very much shaped by its lord and his creator. Adam's endless rage at victor and his inability to act on it always seemed to manifest as the domain's weather, especially on the coast, and Victor's weird muted acceptance of his predicament combined with his obsession with restoring his wife seemed to set the tone for its populace. And the idea of a creature torment by wishing to be something it never can and unable to lash out at the one responsible is so very Gothic. Both Adam and Victor are at once sadly sympathetic figures and just really terrible people. Really, the perfect Darklord.<br /> <br /> With Mordent, I think its character has always been shaped by it essentially being an &quot;artificial&quot; domain brought into Ravenloft by Strahd and Azalin, and then becoming the default lord when they left. On his own, his estate might've just become a pocket domain, but instead its bigger than it should be and so isn't as stamped with his personality. At least that was my take away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T04:08:17-08:00","id":1470416,"title":"","content":"Yeah, changing the Darklord from the Created to the Creator really shifts a lot in the themes of the Domain, which probably also represents the shift in the Domain as a whole- they probably wanted to have a &quot;evil science domain&quot; (likely because of the &quot;agenda reasons&quot; mentioned), and it is hard to do so when the Created is the Darklord because they are the &quot;victim&quot;, which is a very superficial way to treat it, IMO. Frankenstein's monster may have had sympathetic sides, but he still was the monster who tormented his &quot;father&quot; for abandoning him, killing those Frankenstein cared about yet did the monster nothing wrong- which is a dynamic that original Lamordia preserved. The Darklord is the monster, and Mordenheim has no control over the world he basically Created as it is not his story- it is Adam's story, and he is trapped there because it serves Adam's obsession and keeps the show going on. By focusing on Mordenheim as the Darklord, the dynamics is shifted- the obsession of the Creator becomes the driving force of the Domain, and the Created is on the run instead of being an ominous threat in the shadows of the domain, slowly circling around the maker. Which, in a way, feels more like Promethean 2e than the original Mary Shelly's story. Now, it is not that a Domain like that can't work- but it misses the story that Lamordia tried to tell, and I am not sure that the reason to do so was good enough.<br /> <br /> Also, if you may be interested, a <a href=\"https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/dungeons-dragons-dnd-van-richtens-guide-ravenloft-lamordia-frankenstein-preview\" target=\"_blank\">interview </a>about Lamordia before it was released. I don't think it goes into the same depth as the previous one, but it does seem to emphasis that the writers wanted to move away from Frankenstein as the &quot;only inspiration&quot; and cover broader genre- which is probably why they changed the dynamics and the Domain in general<br /> <br /> EDIT: It occurred to me that making such a change would be like turning the Darklord of Barovia from Strahd to Tatyana, where she manipulated the two siblings against each other and now she reincarnates endlessly in an attempt to preserve her power as a queen yet is always doomed to die by Strahd who sincerly loves her which heroically struggles to fight against the curse laid upon him for the murder of his brother, and that Jander was summoned to Ravenloft to recreate the struggle between the brothers, as the writers in this scenario would have wanted to stray from the classical Dracula and Mina dynamics. Like, could it potentially make an interesting Domain if it were to be well written? I think so. Would it be Barovia? <i>Hell no</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-14-2021, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-14T06:27:45-08:00","id":1470426,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a> thank you. This means a lot to me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> agreed. I'll elaborate more on that below.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> the domain you're thinking is probably Paridon, except they focus more on economics and urban violence and less on science itself. It is also home to the Divinity of Mankind, one of the most curious religions in the setting, and the land of the Dread Dopplegangers. Even then, I thoroughly thought while reading Lamordia that they should have done this to Paridon.<br /> <br /> Mordent made sense, but that doesn't change that Godefroy could be improved. And to have the Apparatus as something active, kind of, instead of just an often repeated backdrop no one knows what to do with, was a good addition. Specially if you consider the size of that damn thing, it makes perfect sense for it to still be in Gryphon Manor.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> thank you again for the link. It is far shallower, but again highlights how little the authors understood what they were working with.<br /> <br /> Frankenstein the book is one of the best and most iconic Gothic tales, and the foundation of Gothic Science. The relationship between Creator and Created is extremely complex, and Lamordia kept that and expanded.<br /> <br /> It is an error, though, to think that Lamordia was only a Frankenstein pastiche, because a <b>lot</b> of key elements are distinct and explored upon. Dr. Frankenstein is an obsessed but ultimately kind man, whose moral failing is excusing himself of responsibility under stress, but not doing harm on purpose. He had no direct family and at first no personal drive strong enough to face inconvenience. Under the weight of his sins Frankenstein succumbs with guilty and self-loath, which only drives him further down as he uses his suffering to excuse himself again from action. When he finally goes past this point, it is already too late.<br /> <br /> But Mordenheim is his polar opposite. He have a direct family in the form of Elise and no love for anyone beyond that bond. He sins not because he avoid responsibility, but because he doesn't fucking care, not even enough to say so. Where Frank finds respite on company Mord despises it as undesirable distraction. Where the Creature achieves almost complete power in their relationship, Adam is devoid of power over Mord, with no one to successfully vent his frustration on.<br /> <br /> There's an interesting discussion on the matter in Adam's entry in the Mistipedia. Lamordia <i>does</i> reflect Mordenheim. It does, because Adam's main failing is his jealousy. He envies everything Mordenheim have and is, so his domain mocks him being everything he wants, yet putting his Creator in the position he wishes. Adam is the one avoiding responsibility, as he blames Mordenheim for every facet of his predicament, including his own evil, instead of seeking any remedy by himself (he does have the intelligence to do so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T06:11:06-08:00","id":1470524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470416#post1470416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, could it potentially make an interesting Domain if it were to be well written? I think so. Would it be Barovia? <i>Hell no</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Personally I would prefer for them to just make a new domain than radically retcon and change the most fundamental concepts about older ones. If the authors don't like Lamordia, or find it too constraining or whatever, that's fine. But I think the solution would be to just not write about it and instead make a new domain that reflects what they do want write about. Much better to write a new domain whole cloth than to essentially strip out the entire core identity of an older domain, completely replace everything except for a few names (but hey, go ahead and change those up while you're at it) and then say, &quot;See? It's just like &lt;old thing you enjoyed!&gt;&quot; when it's been so radically changed there's only some vague superficial details left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T08:56:03-08:00","id":1470531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470524#post1470524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Personally I would prefer for them to just make a new domain than radically retcon and change the most fundamental concepts about older ones. If the authors don't like Lamordia, or find it too constraining or whatever, that's fine. But I think the solution would be to just not write about it and instead make a new domain that reflects what they do want write about. Much better to write a new domain whole cloth than to essentially strip out the entire core identity of an older domain, completely replace everything except for a few names (but hey, go ahead and change those up while you're at it) and then say, &quot;See? It's just like &lt;old thing you enjoyed!&gt;&quot; when it's been so radically changed there's only some vague superficial details left.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing that can be done about it. It was evidently some higher decision trickling down in different ways.<br /> <br /> I have Richemulot done and am ready to finish Tepest, but have some other stuff to attend to before I get down to it, so we'll have a short hiatus (a couple days, maybe). But hold on to this thought, because if you think we had horrendous changes until now, you didn't see Richemulot...<br /> <br /> And Tepest will have a lot of changes but some good news, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T18:20:10-08:00","id":1470570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470426#post1470426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the domain you're thinking is probably Paridon, except they focus more on economics and urban violence and less on science itself. It is also home to the Divinity of Mankind, one of the most curious religions in the setting, and the land of the Dread Dopplegangers. Even then, I thoroughly thought while reading Lamordia that they should have done this to Paridon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Checking, it seems the place I was thinking about was Nosos, the final chapter from the original Islands of Terror supplement. The Darklord, Malus Sceleris, is the son of a druid who apparently destroys the local ecosystem like a Captain Planet villain out of spite for his father (who he also murdered). Apparently it was never officially updated after the Domains of Dread hardcover. It strikes me as the sort of domain that probably could've been a good choice for a 5th edition update/overhaul (especially if it drew some inspiration from things like There Will Be Blood, The Harlan County War, or the tv series Deadwood), but oh well. <br /> <br /> Paridon was, IIRC, the one inspired by Victorian London and Jack the Ripper, with its really strict class divisions, and the lower tiers of society being constantly beset by extreme poverty, hunger, crime, and other ills. Sodo, as a doppelg\u00e4nger, always struck me as an unusual choice for the Darklord of such a specific domain. At least until he was specifically identified as Bloody Jack, the Ripper analog, and then it made more sense. Although given some of the side effects of the Fang of the Nosferatu dagger he uses to carry out the murders, I sometimes think a more fitting curse for him would be to no longer have any real existence of his own, instead being just a series of identities he takes on at different times, with none of them remembering who or what he really is (even being the Darklord), save for every 13 years when he becomes Bloody Jack and has some inkling of his true self. <br /> But I confess this is partially motivated by a desire to run a game where the PCs eventually learn that about half their allies and contacts during the adventure are all actually the same person, and that person is the Big Bad. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470524#post1470524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Personally I would prefer for them to just make a new domain than radically retcon and change the most fundamental concepts about older ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally tend to agree. But I say this as a person who is very, very tired of the past decade plus of remakes, retreads, and adaptions in entertainment media, often by people who clearly don't care about much more than cashing in on brand name recognition, and wish more people would take that important risk of creating something new to tell the stories they want to tell. <br /> <br /> I think the best option might've been to just pick about four classic domains (lets say Barovia, Darkon, Lamordia, and maybe either Dementilieu or Mordent, but several others would also work), and present them for the most part as they were in the old material but with the new rules and talk about what new things they new version of Ravenloft might allow you to do with them. Then maybe two to four that are older ones but overhauled and reimagined somewhat. (Tepest? Bluetspur? Sri Raji? G'Henna? The House of Lament?) And then around eight to twelve or more that are entirely new. Including, for example, one with the female mad scientist that's based around ideas of science horror and the like. But that's just how I'd have tried to do it. <br /> <br /> But then I'm also the person who read about the Domains of Delight concept and thought &quot;I want that as its own setting with its own Core and Islands of Ecstasy and clusters and all of that&quot;, because I think a setting that borders on being 'Disney Princesses go on adventures with My Little Ponies' would be an amusing change of pace. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T05:00:04-08:00","id":1470612,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> I thought about Nosos as soon as I hit the post button.<br /> <br /> I usually don't think about it at all, because it is plain bad. But again, that's precisely the reason they could have overhauled it the same way they did with I'Cath and Sri Raji, those are two very good overhauls all things considered, especially I'Cath. Nosos would work wonderfully for both the themes they went in Lamordia and Richemulot (today that one may go out. If not, tomorrow).<br /> <br /> My only qualm with your suggestion for Sodo is that this is already covered in Nova Vaasa by Malken/Hiregaard. And it would bring also a similar question of deciding how much you can ascribe evil and guilt to a mental condition, something I already like how it was done with Tristen. An identity of Sodo that isn't bad still carries his guilt and curse? Does this personality deserves to suffer? Hiregaard has a far better time than Malken, all things considered. He isn't completely unscathed neither completely innocent, but in general had a more fulfilling life than his evil persona, and he fully deserves it as far as he got it.<br /> <br /> Now I'm going to take a look at this Domains of Delight thing, before going to work and then writing our next installment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T05:51:30-08:00","id":1470614,"title":"","content":"Yes, Nosos is a somewhat odd and slightly silly place. It's one of a number of places in Ravenloft that are an interesting idea lacking in execution, IMO. <br /> <br /> As for Sodo, I'd have to try to fully work out the details if I were to actually try such a thing. Likely it might end up as where all of his personas are evil. That and given his back story, perhaps the idea that he can't actually rule his clan directly or something to that effect.<br /> <br /> Domains of Delight are something I only became aware of from DriveThruRPG, where some of them are available as pdf files. I haven't had time to delve into any of it beyond the basic idea that they are apparently to the First World what Domains of Dread are to the Shadow plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T09:17:07-08:00","id":1470715,"title":"","content":"I gave a look at some thing about Domains of Delight, but it seems frankly lacking, which is a shame. They're not so much a counterpart to Ravenloft, but more just closed kingdoms reigned by specific Archfey. If I get the book I may give a more thorough opinion.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>RICHEMULOT</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Simple and short: the Domain of Richemulot was sacrificed for cheap criticism hastily done. There\u2019s nothing worth to see here.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">While in other Domains I could only question their decisions, this one is also objectively badly written. They not only threw aside the old stories and themes of the place, with its horror about the notion of a glass ceiling and corruption beneath a wholesome facade and false meritocracy, to just make a reference to the pandemic. They did it badly.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The text is inconsistent, the references are obvious and thrown around carelessly, there are no clear goals for anyone and the rat theme is played so ridiculously it is comic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I mean it. Jacqueline is using rat slippers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Actually, this whole mess is so thoroughly ridiculous I\u2019m not even angry. The overall description is basic and worthless, three slightly different flavors of quarantine cities and a giant wererat warren, they don\u2019t decide if Jacqueline wants or not to rule, cares or not for the place, or whatever. The adventure ideas are basic or just stupid, including asking the party to be Ace Ventura. The Plague is simple and only scares because they go basically the route of \u201cno matter what a PC does to prevent it, some random shit happens and they get infected\u201d again and again.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Not even the rules for the stages of the epidemic, that should be the heart of the write-up, are salvageable. The four stages are just Nothing Happens and three random encounter tables whose encounters are <u><b>really</b></u> random. The worse the plague gets\u2026 the weirder the tables are. You start with strangers coughing up on you and end up with common rats playing Macbeth in an alley. For real.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>TEPEST</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Here we have something new for this book: Tepest is changed, <u>but not retconned!</u> Well, at least not much.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Most of the Domain\u2019s shtick changed. Out with the Inquisition and the \u201cfairy\u201d hunts, now Viktal is the living trope of the \u201ctoo perfect to be good\u201d village. But instead of things having always been like that, this is actually result of events on old Tepest: the Hag Sisters finally came to blows over something and the youngest came on top. The other two are trapped in the cauldron and Lorinda is <i>de facto</i> the sole Darklord. She went more mad than usual over the idea of having children and started her own independent shenanigans, destroying the other villages in her learning curve of how to become a figure of cult without breaking the toys.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The land outside Viktal don\u2019t have the Inquisition, but still have the old dangers of Tepest, including the fae. Also it has hermits and small bands living outside Lorinda\u2019s direct control. While the biggest changes do not retcon old material, the biggest actual retcon came to avoid change, making Arak an underground kingdom instead of a distinct Domain. Which works, since none of the main rulers of Arak is actually a Darklord anyway. There is a mountain called Gwydion\u2019s Claw, but it is outside the fairies\u2019 reach and they\u2019re worried about that, and only one old human character stays around, now as an undead, so it does imply quite some time has passed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Overall new Tepest works very well. It has a variety of dangers that still exist on their own, unrelated plots to be explored, people to interact. The Inquisition was interesting, but it actually felt one-note unless you explored the fine distinctions between its members, which were meaningless for any group with so much as an Elf or even a Sorcerer. Viktal is presented only in the context of its main plot, but it is actually otherwise quite normal most of the time, so it does serve any purpose a settlement can, only with a little weird colors (and, indeed, with a calm that lets you focus on other things most of the time without making the village an unnecessary hellhole).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Lorinda is all over the place, but not in a too intrusive way. She appears in Viktal at least for the season festivals every three months, is sought off by people for varying reasons, and wanders the place minding her businesses with her Laoirses. Now she even has a Wandering Hut of her own, but fortunately isn\u2019t flying on mortars. There are several ways the characters can meet her. The fairies are still most as they were before, they\u2019re their own thing and are dangerous, but not mindless, and are in conflict with Lorinda. Well done, useful, the tables help and the section on the Tithe can mostly be used just to add spice to the village. I loved it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Wish they had dispensed this treatment to the other domains, Tepest has never been among my favorites.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>VALACHAN</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Welcome to Amazonian Jumanji.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Old Valachan was about conflicting natures. A people that embraces both civilization and survival in the wild, tormented by tyrants that are both predators and tax collectors. The villages aren\u2019t big, but are definitely urban in the midst of the dense forest. Werepanthers and vampires roam the night, calculating their depredations to not come into conflict nor becoming out of prey.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It was a weird place. But a weird place that worked. It was interesting, had variety of things to do and interact with, the dangers of the forest, the plight of its denizens and the social structure and traditions, good and bad. The Darklord was also weird, maybe the weirdest of them all. Von Kharkov had a most strange and convoluted story, and it was even theorized that he was done Darklord less because of his evil (that wasn\u2019t that big for a Darklord, at all) and more because the Dark Powers were curious and amused by his convoluted nature.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Chakuna keeps the strange conditions for being a Darklord despite a lesser evil, yet she is extremely simpler a Darklord and made Valachan an extremely simpler Domain. It is far more reminiscent of the Wildlands, without King Crocodile. The villages exist almost just as a little support for jungle exploration, the forest isn\u2019t temperate anymore, but a rain forest, not even the names of the communities persist except as Easter eggs in the map.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Even despite keeping Kharkov as a character, most of the Domain\u2019s background seems either changed or so distant in the past as to be unrecognizable. Kharkov had his heart ritually ripped and placed in a maze, where Chakuna found it and her heart is there now, they\u2019re not vampires. He was hunting Werepanthers instead of employing them. Apparently things got much more savage and hunt-like way before his deposition. And the land itself is the greater evil, so much so that Chakuna actually chose to be Darklord to keep Valachan from just killing everyone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Not the worse it could be, but I don\u2019t like it. The fact that the inhabitants aren\u2019t necessarily hostile even if they belong to a normally hostile race is interesting, but not enough to change that the entire shtick of the place is that everything else is out to kill you for reasons and Chakuna is a problem just because she hosts the <i>Battle Royale</i>/<i>Hunger Games</i> (I\u2019m one of those people who think HG is just too derivative, but it is better known). It may work for a few sessions, but definitely lacks horror potential. You can increase its usage through the map, at least. Using it as a starting point and figuring out by yourself things for the PCs to do out there actually works better for longer games than the actual write-up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">And next we\u2019ll have the Other Domains. They\u2019re short write-ups, so I\u2019ll have to struggle to keep my comments just as short, but I\u2019ll try so that we can parse all them in one go. Unless people specifically asks for deeper comments based on what I know of their originals.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Typo and formatting 12-17-2021, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T12:05:47-08:00","id":1470726,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the counterpart description was used somewhere - I want to say in a thread on rpg.net - which mentioned them, but in the examples I've seen they look more akin to Alice in Wonderland, Labyrinth, and Legend. But I still want some sort of bright happy counterpart to original Ravenloft and its core, just because I think it would be fun.<br /> <br /> And yes, Richemulot was disappointing. I always rather liked it for its whole &quot;this is fine&quot; attitude, even though everyone was very aware that it wasn't, and there was clearly a lot of rot - physical, social, etc. - under the surface. And I could never in a million years picture Jacqueline wearing anything with a rodent motif, let alone something as tacky as slippers, given the curse she lives under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T11:43:48-08:00","id":1470870,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The Other Domains number 22, some new, some old (For comparison, we just reviewed 17 Domains). Each will get a proper title, a brief impression and my opinion on how interesting and useful it is.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I\u2019ll do this in two installments, though, as I want to deliver the first batch quickly and one of them is expanded on the book and will also be so here. So we have 14 Domains today.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>CYRE 1313</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">A good Pocket Domain is always an interesting addition. The brief description give little to do with the Darklord, but the machine itself is well defined. Easy to use, interesting and versatile.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>FORLORN</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The focus goes on Tristen, which is a shame because that means a huge lot of simplification to fit everything in a single paragraph. There is no description of the domain, so I think it is interesting but lack usefulness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>GHASTRIA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">A bit changed and even more Dorian Grey, but this wasn\u2019t the most complex place to begin with. It focus more on the art and let the orgies to the side, predictable but a shame. As interesting and useful as the original.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>G\u2019HENNA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Some expected retcon, but enough information to be useful, I only think they could have been more directly on saying the people there is starving and the animals are anthropophagi (even herbivores). But good enough.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>INVIDIA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Completely overhauled and ridiculous. The Darklord is the ultimate overbearing mother and the greatest threat is her spoiled child. She\u2019s also dumb, as she summons demons and whatnot to care for the child then doesn\u2019t understand why people don\u2019t want to stay around.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>KEENING</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It lacks direct mention to Tristessa\u2019s child, but otherwise describes her well without dwelling on it too much, so it has some spare text for the domain. Marbh-Cathair isn\u2019t mentioned, but it has a living village of deaf people. As far as it goes, interesting and useful as is.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>KLORR</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">New Domain named after an old character now made Darklord, call it Domain of References. Despite that it is curious and creative enough, too short for so many story hooks. Interesting and useful, but requires more work.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>MARKOVIA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Overhauled by a more direct take on the base themes, but it works well for a short write-up, a scientist getting ever more bestial, worshiped by animals getting ever more intelligent. Good, interesting, useful, easy to apply.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>THE NIGHTMARE LANDS</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Retconned to make Illhousen\u2019s clinic into its center and his lover into the Darklord, and there\u2019s no mention to the Abber Nomads. While it is useful as is, could have been done better and the changes are uninteresting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>NIRANJAN</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">New domain and forms an unofficial cluster with Kalakeri. Plays on themes of brainwashing cults and has a metallic dragon for Darklord as a nice twist. Interesting, easy to use, makes good use of the space given.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>NOVA VAASA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Little to no resemblance to the original, it\u2019s a little twist in the Domain torn by War trope. I like more the duality between Tristen and Malken, but Myar and Malkan work, so I\u2019d say less interesting, but still plenty useful.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>ODIARE/ODAIRE</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Almost no change except the name as above. I know what the old name means, I don\u2019t know what was the problem for the Domain to be so named except for being a weird conjugation. It\u2019s well summed and works.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>THE RIDER\u2019S BRIDGE</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I think this is their third attempt at doing this Domain, first was the Winding Road at 2</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">nd</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> ed, then the Endless Road at 4</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> ed. Made into a Pocket Domain, kept simple and of uncertain origin, useful but predictable.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>RI</b></u></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>SIBILOS</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Now I have to concede, they really dug <b>deep</b> to find this one. The domain itself is completely changed, but the new one works as well as the old one, I think? I mean, it equally doesn\u2019t, yet is as funny a joke, I like it.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T04:45:53-08:00","id":1470924,"title":"","content":"As mentioned earlier, one of the things I really didn't like in this section is that they shoved Sithicus into the &quot;dead domains&quot; territory of Klorr. Like, they have mentioned before the book came out that &quot;Lord Soth's presence will be felt in Ravenloft even though he was freed from the Domain&quot;, and in the end the only thing we got was a &quot;black rose like citadel&quot; getting drawn to its ultimate ruin- which only shows that the team either did not do any research (like reading the actual novel and how Sithicus ended up after Soth left) or that they outright ignored it out of (misguided) thought that the replacement of Soth by Inza was done by the 3e line (the novels predated 3e Ravenloft and Inza as the Darklord was first published in Dragon magazine by the author of the novels), which only emphasize my feeling that they did not do their research- at least, no more than reading a wikipedia article on a very shallow level. <br /> <br /> I mean, sure, they probably left it open ended enough by describing Nedraggard only, and the citadel was consumed by the shadows, but between Klorr being the place where domains go to die and the lack of Sithicus it is clear what their intention was. I guess that between them avoiding 3e Ravenloft and their &quot;relationship&quot; with Dragonlance (especially while the book was written) probably explain why Sithicus was sent into Schrodinger's box- but it is still annoying.. On the other hand, perhaps it was for the best. Who knows how badly Inza would have turned up if they were to write about the Domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T05:06:06-08:00","id":1470927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1470924#post1470924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, sure, they probably left it open ended enough by describing Nedraggard only, and the citadel was consumed by the shadows, but between Klorr being the place where domains go to die and the lack of Sithicus it is clear what their intention was. I guess that between them avoiding 3e Ravenloft and their &quot;relationship&quot; with Dragonlance (especially while the book was written) probably explain why Sithicus was sent into Schrodinger's box- but it is still annoying.. On the other hand, perhaps it was for the best. Who knows how badly Inza would have turned up if they were to write about the Domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Klorr isn't where domains go to die. It contains reflexes of domains destroyed <i>and still existing</i>. And, in the end, it is just another, really weird, domain.<br /> <br /> Not that I disagree with your conclusions and I'm just as annoyed about it all. But then there's Tovag, where things get even worse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T16:35:44-08:00","id":1471166,"title":"","content":"Finally my final post on the Domains. Following that comes the Travelers in the Mists section, where I'll review their take on cross-domain organizations, characters and stuff.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>SCAENA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Simplifying what\u2019s already simple, they not only did unnecessary changes to Lemont\u2019s history, they made his plays American style gorefest horror, which limits tremendously any use for it. Bland, but has enough material.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>SEA OF SORROWS</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Turned into a pocket Domain of sorts, I miss old Van Riese obsession with charting new routes, the new one is a little bland, but it works. The islands remain and I will comment the ones presented, but they\u2019re technically not their own Domains anymore:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- <u><b>Blaustein</b></u>: the same, but Bluebeard was imprisoned by his wives;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- <u><b>Dominia</b></u>: now all the patients are Heinfroth himself through multiple lenses;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- <u><b>Isle of the Ravens</b></u>: brought from the Nocturnal Sea, otherwise unchanged;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- <u><b>The Lighthouse</b></u>: new and interesting, I like the fossil motif;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- <u><b>Vigilant\u2019s Bluff</b></u>: new, interesting and useful to make a safe heaven.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>THE SHADOWLANDS</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It seems more wrong than retconned, due to how much it actually sticks to the original themes, but have to deal with the constraints. It encapsulates the spirit of the Shadowlands Cluster, is interesting, but has little of use for a newcomer.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>SOURAGNE</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Overhauled, now Misroi is an undead prison warden on the lookout for prisoners, and Souragne seems a little more gloom and small, although it may be just an impression. I prefer the old, but this is interesting and good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>STAUNTON BLUFFS</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The only domain that got a new write-up in 4</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> edition, with some retcons. Now it got completely overhauled and is about a Groundhog Day-style ongoing war, with Stonecrest being sacked every day. Interesting, but limited in use.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>TOVAG</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Overwhelmingly stupid. They retconned Vecna\u2019s time in Ravenloft, which is insulting even after all we went through here, and Kas is locked in an eternal war against\u2026 nothing. Imbecilic offensive and useless.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>VHAGE AGENCY</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">New Domain, either Pocket or Island. Extremely derivative, but that works with the word-count constraint, it throws too many loose hooks, so will be a lot of work to use well, but have good potential. Interesting, useful, but hard.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>ZHERISIA</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Shortened, they simplified Timor to place there some random monster they made for this book, and the city is only described as constantly engulfed in riots. Only Sodo himself is more described, acts personally now and eats organs. Lame, easy to use, though.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T17:01:28-08:00","id":1471216,"title":"","content":"I always liked original Zherisia for being a blatant stand and exaggeration of Jack the Ripper's London/Whitechapel, as I thought it worked well for that sort of murder mystery genre, as well as certain Penny Dreadful tropes. Although I sort of wish it and Timor were a city in or on the border of Mordent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-24T20:44:19-08:00","id":1471228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1471216#post1471216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked original Zherisia for being a blatant stand and exaggeration of Jack the Ripper's London/Whitechapel, as I thought it worked well for that sort of murder mystery genre, as well as certain Penny Dreadful tropes. Although I sort of wish it and Timor were a city in or on the border of Mordent.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Merry Christmas! Just arrived from my sister's house (we commemorate Christmas at midnight around here). 1:45 in the morning, I guess it isn't Christmas yet in EST. First post of Christmas for me, anyway.<br /> <br /> I think Paridon works well as an Island, as it's technological stage could be a bit too much for the Core. Also, it certainly plays well with the legendary London fog. But it would be interesting as a part of Mordent, too.<br /> <br /> But Timor, I don't know. While most Conjunction's changes were good, I do miss the original city of Timor and the role of the Queen there.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, focusing on social revolt for Paridon is... a little weird. And they don't even mention it's XIX century feel, or the Divinity of Mankind and its Monks. Really sad choices right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T05:41:32-08:00","id":1471236,"title":"","content":"Feliz Natal. <br /> <br /> If one wanted a domain based on the dark side of social upheaval, revolution, and mob rule, I think Galt from Pathfinder would be a good starting point. It even has guillotines that eat peoples' souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T10:08:13-08:00","id":1471395,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">With the Clusters, Mistways and regular Mist travelers gone, the section on the Travelers makes up for the unifying threads that link the many Domains into a larger setting. Here we have a mixed bag of new and old organizations and characters, with varying degrees of change to the old ones.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Now, overall this section works. We have a broad spectrum of them to keep things interesting in a cross-domain game, but not too much that could make things hard for new players to follow. But they also stretch too much the notion of the Domains as so isolated as the book outright says they are. While this section does not directly contradicts this statement, it seems hard to see them working without breaking it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Keepers of the Feather</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">A mostly rewritten rendition of the</span></span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Keepers of the Black Feather</span></span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> in</span></span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Curse of Strahd</span></span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">, they\u2019re changed even more here. I find it a bit disappointing, because both in the adventure and here this eliminates the only meaningful connection they had to Strahd and the Zarovitches. The original Keepers weren\u2019t necessarily Raven-related, despite many important members being either Wereravens or Ravenkin (a species of intelligent raven without any innate shapeshifting ability), but were linked to Strahd in that their current leader was the last priest of the Sun god of Barovia, Andral, a position Sergei had at the time of his murder. The Holy Symbol of Ravenkind is this god\u2019s symbol originally.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I find the new Keepers and the new history of the Symbol very bland, but the way they\u2019re turned into Travelers is quite curious. Now it is (outside Barovia) a society of occultists mostly driven by curiosity, a reference to the popularization of s\u00e9ances and the like in late XIX century Europe and very reminiscent of Spiritism (my mom\u2019s religion, by the way, so I know it well). The wereravens manipulate the mostly ignorant society from afar, yet the Keepers do get their hands in a number of real stuff and have the Rookeries, through which they manage the most trustworthy cross-domain communications system. Okay, I guess?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Vistani</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On one hand, they undid the previous retcon they had done in 4</span><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">th</span></sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> edition. Instead of planar travelers, here the Vistani are strictly described as a Ravenloft phenomena. They hail from Barovia\u2019s original world, but now are adapted to the Mists. Also, instead of just saying they\u2019re a culture without ties to species, they settle for stating that the Vistani incorporate a few traveling companions, it is rare, but enough that while they\u2019re mostly human, you\u2019ll find the odd non-human Vistani here and there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">For me, that works splendidly well. Opening the Vistani just this little bit is a long shot at making them better to integrate into a game, add some variety and explain out some official characters (like the Halfling Vistana Luba) without making them too generic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">But on the other hand, they avoid depicting the Vistani as either being mistrusted or deserving it like the plague, and I think it has two major drawbacks. First, it outright went from racism because they\u2019re mostly shady people to racism because they\u2019re too idealized. People who suffer from racism know well how both can be horrible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Here they went so far that they outright stripped the Radanaviches from Vistani status. Now they are presented as a family of criminals that pretended to be Vistani, and Ezmeralda is a Vistani only through adoption. Utterly ridiculous, only Madame Eva is kept as a somewhat shady Vistana, and even her isn\u2019t described as certainly an evil one, she may be just mysterious. And Hyskosa is now outright a hero...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The greatest harm to their own depiction, though, is that the Vistani are described as regulars everywhere, not a constant or predictable sight, but frequent enough for everyone to know about them and expect to trade with them. That makes it really hard to swallow that people don\u2019t believe or are curious about other Domains if they know for a fact those Mist wanderers exist and bring news and goods from other lands.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Church of Ezra</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">From all religions in the setting Ezra used to be the most spread and, despite many schisms, it was interesting in how much contact the sects of the church had. If this was kept somehow, it would be really interesting. But instead it is just a paragraph to repeat that it doesn\u2019t happen and in each Domain it is its own thing. Why is this even here, then?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>The Circle</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Simplified and made more stupid, IMO. The tragedy of the Knights of the Shadow was exchanged for a version that instead acts like the most straightforward stereotype of Lawful Good = Lawful Stupid, being in many ways the exact opposite of what the Circle was in Ravenloft (or even in their original world). They\u2019re also stripped of their more varied membership to be just a bunch of knights from the Shadowlands instead of pilgrimaging there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>The Kargat and the Kargatane</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Not much to say about these. They\u2019re pretty much the same, described without much detail, but given enough information about. It does mention their current status as fractious groups warring for the benefit of the factions described in Darkon\u2019s write-up. What just isn\u2019t explained at all, though, is why they are a cross-domain thing and what they do with it, as neither this or Darkon\u2019s write-up give any benefit to be so obtained for them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Order of the Guardians</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Same as ever, it received a rather grandiose description with little detail, I think it could be better done, but not a bad one, though. They at least make sense even with the more closed domains of this book.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Priests of Osybus</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">A completely new faction of soul-stealing immortals trying to free Strahd from Ravenloft. I think it holds enough novelty to be interesting, although it seems we\u2019ll have to wait another chapter to get a more thorough depiction on them, and I think other factions here could have used that benefit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Ulmist Inquisition</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Same as above, new and described later, but we got a glimpse of a society of Psionic Paladins that are feared for not being very keen on the notion of privacy. Interesting, I\u2019m curious now to see them further.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Now, originally I was going to post all the comments on this section at once, but as this is taking more time to write than predicted (\u2018cause life things to do), I\u2019ll finish with the individual characters later.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Formatting 12-28-2021, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T15:22:58-08:00","id":1471505,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Alanik Ray and Arthur Sedg</b></u></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>(e)</b></u></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>wick</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Ravenloft\u2019s main Holmes &amp; Watson rip-off finally married! There\u2019s a little retcon in that they mashed-up Alanik\u2019s time in Mordent with his later period as constable, making everything happen at Martira Bay, but otherwise this short write-up advanced their story more than changed anything. They also changed Arthur\u2019s name, but\u2019 is so minor I see it more as a typo. Ray is in a wheelchair now, but as result of an accident, so I don\u2019t see a problem, and they formalized they\u2019re a gay couple, no one became a woman here. They moved to Port-a-Lucine, and the only question remaining is again the same: how does they work in such a closed-domains setting?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>The Caller</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Since they retconned Isolde so thoroughly, they should have just ditched the Gentleman Caller entirely. They got rid of its main MO, what\u2019s left is utterly generic. Making it change sex at ease isn\u2019t a problem, I don\u2019t see the character getting any weaker if sometimes it bears children itself. With this, a host of characters got harmed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Erasmus van Richten</b></u></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">and</span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Ez d\u2019Avenir</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Linked by the retcons in Rudolph\u2019s backstory. Instead of trapped in Richten Haus, Erasmus\u2019 ghost accompanies the father around, communicating with his associates. Ezmeralda is a new character from CoS, the child of the Radanaviches, now further retconned to only become a true Vistana later in life. They\u2019re interesting, but I think there were better options for this section instead of deepening here the connections of van Richten. TBH, the whole van Richten presence in CoS was more than a little unnecessary for me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Firan Zal\u2019Honan</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Here you are! Now, this is an Easter Egg I really, really liked! The author here either was one of the few that cared for reading the 1996 novel <i>King of the Dead</i> or, more likely, read the Mistipedia on Azalin Rex to find about his identity prior to coming to Ravenloft. That\u2019s a nice change of pace, and the write-up is full of references and, at the same time, interesting and useful on its own if you want to keep Firan as a distinct character or just didn\u2019t get the connection.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Jander Sunstar</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Protagonist of the very first Ravenloft novel, <i>Vampire of the Mists</i>, Jander is among the longest standing heroes of Ravenloft despite being a vampire and having the accompanying dark impulses. Most of the time he tries to do good and either leave his victims alive or prey on the irredeemable. Why on Earth dd they had to change him into being darker and edgier!?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">And the changes are just stupid, they\u2019re not simpler than what originally happened, just hollower of meaning or purpose. This very book muses about the possibility of making Tatyana reincarnate outside the Mists, then the character that was one such incarnation gets changed to just a random adventurer. All his original story hooks aren\u2019t just ignored, but completely unmade, and in their place are thrown two hooks that could have been put here anyway without this, aren\u2019t that clever and aren\u2019t that developed to matter.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Larissa Snowmane</b></u></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><b>(and </b></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Nathan Timothy</b></u></i></span></span></i><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><b>)</b></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Remembering Larissa was a good one. There\u2019s some built-in reluctance with her past that I find odd for her, but overall the write-up is ok. They even acknowledge the origin of her <i>Dance of the Dead</i>, despite no mentions in Souragne\u2019s write-up (Misroi taught her, in the novel he didn\u2019t felt unpaid at all). Citing she\u2019s in her 60s already is also nice, although it may confuse people about her hair (it was always white).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">A major nitpick is that they focused on making Souragne a plot hook as if she had unfinished business there, while they cited Nathan and didn\u2019t develop further about him. That\u2019s extremely unfair with both characters, with her for ignoring the conclusion of her story, with Nathan for not giving attention to the only \u201credeemed\u201d Darklord I remember.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Rudolph van Richten</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">By the might of the Olympians, what\u2019s this!? Disney doesn\u2019t tone down fairy tales as much as they toned down Rudolph\u2019s backstory, and I\u2019m serious! It is the same basic story, but reworked all over the place to remove the unsavory parts. Remove the unsavory parts from the BG of a monster hunter in a horror-themed book. As said earlier, the Radanaviches are made into fake Vistani and common criminals. Van Richten refuses to treat the injured member because they\u2019re criminals. He dismantles their operation. Irena goes to jail. Baron Metus just kills Erasmus, and his mother for good measure. Irena\u2019s curse works for reasons, but after his family no one else was ever a victim of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Da fuck. This makes little to no sense, it is utter bullshit. They retconned his death, then put him in CoS, now this!? What\u2019s wrong with them!?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>The Weathermay-Foxgrove Twins</b></u></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Continuing the trend set with their uncle, the twins got their story made happier to some extent. Now there is no familial strain or worry, Rudolph and George both were completely supportive of two teenagers deciding to train as monster hunters, because their mother apparently has nothing better to wish for her daughters. Since their \u201cuncle Rudolph\u201d didn\u2019t disappeared for good, they follow his steps just because saying your uncle\u2019s fianc\u00e9 is a monster and being right proves you can handle this life and be a happy person.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">No, it doesn\u2019t even has nothing to do with Gennifer being possibly infected. This is just a side note. Also, she is a Druid now, because she learned with Rudolph, that is a Priest now, and it makes sense, really, of course. The following art of a Keeper\u2019s S\u00e9ance going to shit is pretty good, though, and capture very well the group\u2019s feel.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">My main complain here is how little the write-ups of those groups and characters follow the proposed tone this book ascribes to the setting. Even the new characters and groups, or the ones most changed, are far closer to the old setting, with a Core and clusters and known Mistways and regular trade among Domains, than to a take where all Domains are even more isolated and don\u2019t even know about one another. They not just thread through the Mists, they do so as if this was mundane. Which it used to be, more or less.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The Keepers have reliable communication, Vistani are regular inter-domain traders. At least six organizations are immersed in regular cross-domain activities, and the folk wandering the Mists aren\u2019t just secret monster hunters and shady Archmages, but also Private Eyes and good-standing citizens that fully expect to return from a trip across the Mists in time to keep mundane businesses going.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">While I approve this take more than the officially stated one, this inconsistency is serious. Or rather, this consistent disregard in one large section for the themes and tone of the others.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">On our next post I\u2019ll take another detour. Chapter 4 is advice for running horror games, I want to save it for the end. I\u2019ll decide if I\u2019ll do chapter 5, where there\u2019s a promise of doing monsters and explaining the Osybus and Ulmist, or if I\u2019ll go to the beginning of the book and read what they actually propose for character creation. Any thoughts, people?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Formatting 12-30-2021, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T18:08:21-08:00","id":1471515,"title":"","content":"A bunch of the more frustrating things in this book seem to come from this impulse of either wanting it both ways or just not even being able to be consistent in tone/approach. They edge Jander on up, yet at the same time change Van Richten and the Foxgrove Twins in the way they do. There's no seeming rhyme or reason to it.<br /> <br /> Wanting to treat characters and organizations as moving between the domains in an interconnected way, yet basically sundering the idea of connections between the domains otherwise (again, not even a demiplane of its own anymore, let alone a world), feels badly jangled and difficult to find a consistent feel in.<br /> <br /> Also yes, they did the Circle dirty, as the kids say, and seeming for not much more reason than to get to throw in a mocking &quot;lol, teh lawful good is teh stupide!!1 derp derp.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T09:56:33-08:00","id":1471540,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Jander's writeup made me really cringe. I don't get why they changed his story to make him so &quot;evil&quot;. I remember that in his first iteration in 5e (Descent of Avernus iirc), WotC suffered from a backlash for how they treated Jander that even the original writer of the novel said &quot;it is not Jander&quot;, so they added this &quot;plothook&quot; about there being multitude of Janders. Really, I can't get WHY they edged him so much? Why to take the tragic hero and make him so unsympathetic, removing everything which made him interesting and leaving just a hollow cringe shell? It feels like they decided that they need to give reasons for players to kill him without feeling regret- which just makes me feel like the writer simply didn't like Ravenloft. Vampire of the Mists is the first Ravenloft novel, and it is almost quintessential for feeling what the setting is all about IMO. Those revisions are kicking the original setting where it hurts, and for me shows how the writers really either didn't like the game or worse, didn't care.<br /> <br /> Because of that, I was terrified of seeing what they planned on doing to Larissa, but fortunately she survived almost unscathed. Sure, there is the strange thing about a &quot;debt&quot; which makes no sense (I think that Misroi stated that the undead she created are his &quot;payment&quot;, and let's be honest- if the fate of Willen does not cover the debt I don't know what would). In short, I really feel like I have little to no value from this book- some parts of it I found useful, especially the mechanics like new player options and such, but really I am going to ignore the vast majority of it without a second thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T00:03:53-08:00","id":1471648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1471540#post1471540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Those revisions are kicking the original setting where it hurts, and for me shows how the writers really either didn't like the game or worse, didn't care.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In short, I really feel like I have little to no value from this book- some parts of it I found useful, especially the mechanics like new player options and such, but really I am going to ignore the vast majority of it without a second thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please give an opinion on what you think about this method for multi-quoting. We have to be creative here.<br /> <br /> On the matter of the authors, what is really clear to me is that they are many, actually, and this team wasn't exactly on the same page. A lot of things stink of editorial order, but the general lack of cohesiveness on how to treat previous material shows that they had many hands on deck and few to no oversight on what those hands were doing. Or if there was, this oversight purposefully chose to not care about old stuff.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't say I have little use for this. There are many good ideas and good write-ups in the middle of all the bad stuff and Ravenloft <b>is</b> the kind of fluid setting where I can easily implement the bits I like without hurting the whole as much as they did. So I'd say that, while I really am furious about what they did in general, the book <b>is </b>useful.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, though, for their utter lack of respect with the fanbase and what I thoroughly perceive as false advertising (this is <b><u><i>not</i></u></b> Ravenloft as expected by the consumer), I'm thinking seriously about a lawsuit against them if they don't refund me. I am <b><u>this</u></b> pissed off. If I have to give the book back, so be it, but I don't want my money on their hands for this.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">My final decision was for chapter 5. I took a cursory look and will be a relatively short text for the entire chapter as it\u2019s simple and not that long anyway. It starts with some notes on using and tweaking monsters for horror and then goes for write-ups and stats, including the two new groups, Osybus and Ulmists.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><u><b>HORROR MONSTERS</b></u></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">First part, tips on making monsters horrifying, even known monsters. A quick presentation and then they cut to the chase, that\u2019s a positive thing. They define six techniques to achieve this and describe then at some length: <i><u><b>origin</b></u></i>, <i><u><b>notoriety</b></u></i>, <i><u><b>description</b></u></i>, <i><u><b>tactics</b></u></i>, <i><u><b>traits</b></u></i> and <i><u><b>minions</b></u></i>.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The techniques are indeed simple and straightforward, and generally good advice. <i><u><b>Origin</b></u></i> is to use a stat block with a creature with completely distinct background, good advice and delivered ok. <i><u><b>Notoriety</b></u></i> is the extremely valid advice to make a monster\u2019s reputation precede it, but constructed out of witness ignorance, a notion many GMs slip on, so that\u2019s really good.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Description</b></u></i> is three clear techniques to make engaging descriptions, could have been better phrased, but isn\u2019t bad. <i><u><b>Tactics</b></u></i> is about making the monster behave creatively in combat and I think it is still very obscure in how it was written, but is a harder topic to explore in so few words. <i><u><b>Traits</b></u></i> is the suggestion of borrowing or creating new traits to a stat block, good advice, but very generic, I felt a lack of focus on how to do this for horror, but the examples kind of do that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i><u><b>Minions</b></u></i> is a bunch of new traits to add to minions of greater evils, and here I think they could seriously have done a better job, it feels unnecessarily focused on servitors and four out of five are more cool powers than horror tropes. Given context it really misses the mark, except for the first one, <i><b>Alien Mind</b></i>, obvious but valid.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Closing the section they put the advice to work on a sample creation, the Bagman, and I must say that I liked it. The creature is cool and stands on its own, and the process is described well enough to showcase the advice working. The end result has the stats of a Troll, but twisted into a cursed adventurer that now slips out of bags and other adventure equipment in its maddened search for home, randomly traversing the cracks of reality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">An important trait they should have put in the <i><u><b>minions</b></u></i> subsection, and one they use a lot themselves, is simply immortality. Making monsters immortal, so that they can\u2019t be definitely eliminated just through combat, is really a simple but effective way to emphasize horror without making them more dangerous for the PCs. As a general note, in a horror-themed game combat shouldn\u2019t solve problems, even in D&amp;D. It should certainly happen, but <b>by itself</b> the more you avoid it as <i><b>conflict resolution</b></i>, the better. And making the enemy immortal, so that only an appropriate themed action, decision or achievement can resolve the conflict, is a simple, easy to apply tool for that. While they don\u2019t gave this advice they use it, and the Bagman is one such monster.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I\u2019ll let it here for now, next will be the general write-ups for most monsters. We have newcomers and old folk, some just upgraded for the new edition, some quite changed. They\u2019ll have a quick summary of my opinion, in a similar fashion to the <i><u><b>Other Domains</b></u></i>, but I\u2019ll take my time on some of them. Probably I\u2019ll let Priests of Osybus and Ulmist Inquisition for the end, because they have more impact elsewhere so they have a duty to be better written.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Some italicization. 01-02-2022, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T09:02:25-08:00","id":1471669,"title":"","content":"Regarding Tactics, I'm reminded of the bit from the original Ravenloft adventure module, where it said for the DM to run Strahd as they would a PC. Which I interpreted to mean A) be familiar with his stats and abilities and try to use them in the same clever ways PCs use theirs, and B) have him be active with his own plots and movements that advance his own agenda beyond just reacting to the PCs presence. <br /> <br /> With the idea of Immortality, from a Pathfinder perspective, I keep coming back to the idea of the Darklords (and certain other characters and monsters) having Mythic levels. In the case of the Darklords, their mythic paths are probably the corrupted versions mentioned in Horror Adventures (Butcher, Heretic, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T22:31:01-08:00","id":1471717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1468961-ravenloft-5th-edition-review?p=1471648#post1471648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the matter of the authors, what is really clear to me is that they are many, actually, and this team wasn't exactly on the same page. A lot of things stink of editorial order, but the general lack of cohesiveness on how to treat previous material shows that they had many hands on deck and few to no oversight on what those hands were doing. Or if there was, this oversight purposefully chose to not care about old stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my takeaway too. Poor editorial oversight, and they weren't clear to the authors about how the setting had changed. Also it felt like in some of the places authors were basically allowed to do whatever they wanted, previous material be damned, and that freedom led to some weird, out-of-place stuff like Richemulot where Jacqueline wears rat slippers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T14:35:19-07:00","id":1476533,"title":"","content":"Hopefully all of this isn't a bad sign for the pending Dragonlance book... It probably is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}